WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:01:12.878 --> 00:01:14.833
<i>If I had a son,</i>


00:01:15.545 --> 00:01:19.538
<i>what would I tell
him as a welcome to this world?</i>


00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.495
<i>Perhaps I would just describe
an evening, nothing else.</i>


00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.910
<i>An evening on my boat,</i>


00:01:30.295 --> 00:01:32.701
<i>this heavy, well-built freighter</i>


00:01:33.378 --> 00:01:36.543
<i>which at any moment can become
a fragile, tiny shell</i>


00:01:36.753 --> 00:01:39.206
<i>compared to the forces
of the sea beneath it.</i>


00:01:41.545 --> 00:01:44.211
<i>I would tell him about
this man's world of mine...</i>


00:01:45.878 --> 00:01:49.410
<i>the monotony of the work,
the simple food,</i>


00:01:50.253 --> 00:01:52.659
<i>the rare moments of delirium in the harbors...</i>


00:01:53.795 --> 00:01:56.413
<i>the beauty of sleeping under the stars.</i>


00:01:58.211 --> 00:02:01.210
<i>I would tell him about that constant alertness,</i>


00:02:01.753 --> 00:02:05.083
<i>towards the slightest
changes of the rambling waves</i>


00:02:06.461 --> 00:02:08.370
<i>which can take your life so easily,</i>


00:02:08.503 --> 00:02:10.209
<i>without any bad intention...</i>


00:02:11.253 --> 00:02:14.003
<i>I would tell him about our life...</i>


00:02:14.878 --> 00:02:17.829
<i>trying to control the uncontrollable...</i>


00:04:20.795 --> 00:04:22.454
Hey, easy now!


00:04:22.711 --> 00:04:24.122
Keep it steady!


00:04:24.503 --> 00:04:25.665
Got it.


00:04:56.503 --> 00:04:56.918
Yes.


00:05:03.003 --> 00:05:04.293
- Thank you, Tommy.
- Should I?


00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:05.368
No, it's fine.


00:05:33.586 --> 00:05:34.997
Here he is, sir!


00:05:35.378 --> 00:05:36.374
Thank you Tommy.


00:05:38.378 --> 00:05:40.369
Was there something wrong
with the food, sir?


00:05:41.003 --> 00:05:43.575
I've got a stomachache, Habib. Again.


00:05:45.086 --> 00:05:49.163
May I ask, is it a bloated feeling,
or is it like a stone?


00:05:50.253 --> 00:05:51.912
Like a stone. Exactly.


00:05:53.211 --> 00:05:54.871
What about smoking?


00:05:55.586 --> 00:05:56.831
Not even that helps...


00:05:59.003 --> 00:06:00.165
What is it?


00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.545
<i>Is it the seaman's illness?</i>


00:06:02.711 --> 00:06:04.086
I'm afraid so, sir.


00:06:05.711 --> 00:06:07.122
I'm terribly sorry,
sir, but...


00:06:07.503 --> 00:06:09.209
no wonder after all these years.


00:06:09.545 --> 00:06:12.163
Well then...
You're as fit as a butcher's dog.


00:06:13.086 --> 00:06:14.413
But I'm married.


00:06:15.086 --> 00:06:15.668
And?


00:06:16.628 --> 00:06:17.659
It helps.


00:07:16.586 --> 00:07:19.786
Have you gone mad asking me
to meet you in this fancy place?


00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:22.493
Just sit down and be quiet.


00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:25.995
Kodor, you're nuts...


00:07:27.461 --> 00:07:28.244
Hey!


00:07:28.503 --> 00:07:29.830
What are you drinking?


00:07:31.128 --> 00:07:32.787
I will have a glass of milk.


00:07:33.336 --> 00:07:34.996
Something's wrong
with my stomach.


00:07:35.836 --> 00:07:36.832
Aha.


00:07:37.586 --> 00:07:40.158
But please, order something else!


00:07:40.461 --> 00:07:43.377
Something normal.
I don't want to create a scene here.


00:07:43.961 --> 00:07:45.621
A coffee for him!


00:07:48.586 --> 00:07:51.336
Don't look over there and speak softly.


00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:55.285
My business partner is betraying me
right here and right now.


00:07:55.836 --> 00:07:57.117
I see.


00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:01.752
No, no, no, don't look over there!
Look at me.


00:08:02.253 --> 00:08:04.955
Make like you're chatting.
Huh? Chit-chat chit-chat...


00:08:06.253 --> 00:08:07.912
Uhm, alright.


00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:10.829
I've decided to get married.


00:08:12.628 --> 00:08:14.916
And who are you going to marry?


00:08:15.378 --> 00:08:17.251
I don't know yet. A woman.


00:08:18.003 --> 00:08:19.460
She won't see
much of me anyway.


00:08:19.711 --> 00:08:22.378
Hah, it's a bit tricky like that!


00:08:22.753 --> 00:08:25.503
I could marry the first woman
who comes in through that door.


00:08:25.711 --> 00:08:27.620
It's easy to say.


00:08:27.795 --> 00:08:29.501
They're shaking hands.


00:08:29.836 --> 00:08:31.661
It seems they are leaving.


00:08:34.795 --> 00:08:36.454
The swine.


00:08:38.586 --> 00:08:40.744
I'll make him eat his own shit!


00:08:41.711 --> 00:08:43.584
Now, let's see!


00:08:45.961 --> 00:08:46.660
What?


00:08:47.628 --> 00:08:49.951
You said you'd marry
the first one to come in. Right?


00:08:50.211 --> 00:08:51.159
Yeah...


00:08:51.711 --> 00:08:53.584
It was just a figure of speech.


00:08:54.003 --> 00:08:55.579
I knew you'd back out of it.


00:09:04.961 --> 00:09:06.668
That was a close one.


00:09:07.253 --> 00:09:08.829
You escaped by a cunthair.


00:09:09.503 --> 00:09:10.416
Go to hell.


00:09:10.795 --> 00:09:12.454
But tell me the truth.


00:09:13.295 --> 00:09:16.210
This whole marriage business...
aren't you afraid?


00:09:17.586 --> 00:09:18.701
Of what?


00:09:19.045 --> 00:09:21.035
What if she cheats on you for example?


00:09:21.628 --> 00:09:22.706
Won't that bother you?


00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:24.709
It's part of the deal.


00:09:27.961 --> 00:09:29.336
Ah! Listen...


00:09:29.795 --> 00:09:32.746
Could you help me out?
I'm a bit short on money.


00:09:37.878 --> 00:09:39.040
Thank you.


00:09:43.545 --> 00:09:44.742
Ciao Jakob!


00:09:46.086 --> 00:09:47.876
Thank you for the drink!


00:11:02.836 --> 00:11:04.412
Forgive my intrusion.


00:11:05.795 --> 00:11:08.082
Alright. But make it short.


00:11:11.086 --> 00:11:13.457
Please be my wife.


00:11:15.170 --> 00:11:16.829
I'm dead serious.


00:11:41.253 --> 00:11:44.749
I can imagine how weird it must seem
to you that someone just...


00:11:44.878 --> 00:11:46.205
walks up to
your table and...


00:11:46.295 --> 00:11:48.168
Tell me something about yourself.


00:11:48.253 --> 00:11:49.119
Quickly...


00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:52.408
Well, I'm a sea captain.


00:11:53.086 --> 00:11:55.326
I'm six feet tall.


00:11:55.461 --> 00:11:57.619
Yeah I can see how tall you are.


00:11:57.920 --> 00:11:59.377
When is our wedding?


00:11:59.795 --> 00:12:00.743
Tomorrow?


00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:03.586
Let's say in a week.
That sounds more realistic.


00:12:05.295 --> 00:12:06.705
I'm quiet serious.


00:12:07.378 --> 00:12:09.037
Don't spoil the game.


00:12:10.586 --> 00:12:12.246
What sort of captain
did you say you are?


00:12:12.961 --> 00:12:14.621
I haven't said yet...


00:12:16.378 --> 00:12:19.459
Freighter. Bulk cargo, generally.


00:12:20.503 --> 00:12:21.878
And is that interesting?


00:12:22.211 --> 00:12:26.419
Well, it depends on the cargo.
For example, coming from...


00:12:26.503 --> 00:12:27.960
Your name, quickly!


00:12:28.295 --> 00:12:29.954
Captain Jakob Störr.


00:12:34.211 --> 00:12:36.285
Lizzy! My dear!


00:12:38.253 --> 00:12:39.912
I'm a bit late, forgive me!


00:12:40.128 --> 00:12:41.890
Let me introduce you,
gentlemen!


00:12:42.045 --> 00:12:43.325
Mr. Ridolfi.


00:12:43.670 --> 00:12:45.329
Captain Jakob...


00:12:46.295 --> 00:12:47.954
- Störr...
- Störr.


00:12:48.503 --> 00:12:49.700
Mon fiancée.


00:12:51.461 --> 00:12:52.706
Well...


00:12:53.628 --> 00:12:54.873
Congratulations.


00:12:55.711 --> 00:12:57.916
Wasn't this a bit...


00:12:58.086 --> 00:12:58.869
sudden?


00:13:00.045 --> 00:13:01.584
He's a sea captain,
you know.


00:13:02.378 --> 00:13:03.623
How romantic.


00:13:03.878 --> 00:13:06.082
A profession that breaks
women's hearts.


00:13:07.336 --> 00:13:09.292
By the way,
you're not afraid of him?


00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:11.996
Just a teeny little bit.


00:13:12.628 --> 00:13:16.705
In this case may I be your witness,
my dear, as your most loyal friend?


00:13:18.628 --> 00:13:21.579
I'm sorry my sweet, you must
come up with someone else.


00:13:23.128 --> 00:13:25.332
Do you object to
my humble person, sir?


00:13:27.170 --> 00:13:28.118
No.


00:13:29.295 --> 00:13:31.997
But I don't think you'll be recovered
and back on your feet by then.


00:13:36.378 --> 00:13:37.326
Lizzy?


00:13:42.628 --> 00:13:43.790
See you later.


00:13:44.628 --> 00:13:45.594
Bye.


00:13:55.795 --> 00:13:57.643
You are
some piece of work.


00:13:57.920 --> 00:13:58.785
So are you.


00:14:01.128 --> 00:14:02.373
I mean, uhm...


00:14:55.045 --> 00:14:56.290
You know what?


00:15:00.628 --> 00:15:04.326
Let's have some food brought up,
and I'll teach you sailor's poker. Alright?


00:15:09.586 --> 00:15:11.293
This fish is good!


00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:14.042
I'm surprised you can get it in Paris.


00:15:14.628 --> 00:15:16.702
It would do in any harbor tavern.


00:15:18.128 --> 00:15:21.245
Oh, you just have a healthy appetite.


00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:25.332
Yeah.


00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:27.127
Did I say something funny?


00:15:27.628 --> 00:15:28.624
No.


00:15:29.378 --> 00:15:30.658
No. It's just that...


00:15:31.795 --> 00:15:33.170
Never mind!


00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:36.917
So...


00:15:39.795 --> 00:15:41.075
Sailor's poker then?


00:15:47.045 --> 00:15:50.375
Actually there's a special version of this.


00:15:50.711 --> 00:15:51.992
Would you
like to learn it?


00:15:52.878 --> 00:15:54.158
Sure. How does it go?


00:15:57.295 --> 00:16:00.625
That's what we play when
there are ladies in our company.


00:16:01.045 --> 00:16:02.538
Come on, tell me.


00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:06.458
Uhm... the one who loses...


00:16:07.711 --> 00:16:09.371
takes off a piece of clothing.


00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:16.959
Ah, it was a stupid idea.


00:16:19.628 --> 00:16:21.999
So that's how you pass
your time on dry land.


00:16:23.961 --> 00:16:25.242
Good to know.


00:16:31.295 --> 00:16:32.575
Forget it.


00:16:37.378 --> 00:16:39.582
Let's give it a try.
I don't mind.


00:16:43.836 --> 00:16:45.117
Alright.


00:16:49.336 --> 00:16:51.624
So, poker goes like this...


00:16:52.128 --> 00:16:53.953
I know how to play poker.


00:17:36.795 --> 00:17:37.909
This is great.


00:17:39.545 --> 00:17:41.832
I never dreamed of such
a funny wedding night.


00:17:50.253 --> 00:17:52.541
Come now, stop sulking.


00:17:53.545 --> 00:17:55.535
It was your idea, wasn't it?


00:18:28.628 --> 00:18:30.453
You sure know how to kiss.


00:18:32.795 --> 00:18:35.082
How large is your base for comparison?


00:18:37.086 --> 00:18:38.544
Don't spoil it.


00:19:22.378 --> 00:19:24.251
I'll be back in four months.


00:19:27.086 --> 00:19:29.374
Would be nice if this really worked out.


00:19:29.836 --> 00:19:31.827
Yes, it would.


00:19:45.128 --> 00:19:46.585
Don't worry!


00:19:46.753 --> 00:19:48.210
I'll wait for you.


00:21:44.295 --> 00:21:45.326
This is nice.


00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:00.498
Hello.


00:22:01.711 --> 00:22:03.252
Hello captain.


00:22:05.170 --> 00:22:06.876
I brought you something.


00:22:16.420 --> 00:22:17.747
You remembered.


00:22:17.961 --> 00:22:19.123
Of course.


00:22:21.670 --> 00:22:23.045
Thank you.


00:24:12.170 --> 00:24:13.959
Lizzy, finally!


00:24:15.253 --> 00:24:16.415
Hello.


00:24:16.586 --> 00:24:19.621
Let me introduce
our Lizzy's husband,


00:24:19.920 --> 00:24:22.586
who is finally back from his voyage
and is able to join us.


00:24:22.878 --> 00:24:24.253
- Good evening.
- Welcome.


00:24:25.920 --> 00:24:26.819
So...


00:24:26.920 --> 00:24:31.543
Let me introduce... Madeleine, Paul,
Henriette, Maurice,


00:24:32.170 --> 00:24:32.952
Geneviève...


00:24:33.170 --> 00:24:34.497
And so Jacques...


00:24:34.670 --> 00:24:38.415
And Pierre! I always forget him,
I don't know why...


00:24:39.586 --> 00:24:41.625
And so Jacques travels on the oceans,


00:24:41.753 --> 00:24:44.455
to bring us stories that
we can't wait to hear.


00:24:45.128 --> 00:24:45.792
Right?


00:24:46.170 --> 00:24:47.663
That always fascinated me.


00:24:48.128 --> 00:24:49.752
Travelling...


00:24:50.711 --> 00:24:51.790
I'll leave you to it...


00:25:00.128 --> 00:25:02.534
I always wanted to find out...


00:25:04.336 --> 00:25:06.659
why a ship doesn't sink?


00:25:08.461 --> 00:25:10.002
It's unbelievable...


00:25:10.420 --> 00:25:12.743
I know I sound stupid, but...


00:25:13.628 --> 00:25:15.750
the whole thing is made of iron,


00:25:16.586 --> 00:25:19.585
plus people, cargo...


00:25:20.878 --> 00:25:24.623
some ships even transport stones,
so how does it work?


00:25:27.045 --> 00:25:30.126
Uhm, I'll try to explain it,
it's the law of physics.


00:25:31.378 --> 00:25:33.084
Yes of course,
the laws of physics, but...


00:25:33.211 --> 00:25:35.534
I don't know anything about physics.


00:25:35.836 --> 00:25:39.285
Listen I asked him something
completely stupid...


00:25:40.003 --> 00:25:42.374
Why ships don't sink...


00:26:56.836 --> 00:26:58.496
Excuse me, Sir,
but well...


00:26:58.795 --> 00:26:59.411
Kodor is here.


00:26:59.545 --> 00:27:00.790
I'm eating,
let him wait.


00:27:01.045 --> 00:27:02.585
Alright. I'm sorry...


00:27:02.670 --> 00:27:04.578
Let me in, let me in... Hey!


00:27:06.545 --> 00:27:08.535
Go on, go on! Eat!


00:27:09.503 --> 00:27:12.122
I wouldn't want to disturb you
for all the world.


00:27:14.961 --> 00:27:16.419
I've got some goods.


00:27:17.670 --> 00:27:19.127
A bit of hashish.


00:27:19.878 --> 00:27:21.952
The fella's in a bind.
You can have it cheap.


00:27:22.170 --> 00:27:23.829
Aren't you that fella
by any chance?


00:27:23.920 --> 00:27:26.291
Why, was somebody telling you stories?


00:27:27.128 --> 00:27:28.290
Forget it, I'm fine.


00:27:29.336 --> 00:27:30.996
I'm in excellent shape...


00:27:33.420 --> 00:27:35.126
We can go halves,


00:27:35.795 --> 00:27:37.501
I feel like being generous today.


00:27:39.378 --> 00:27:40.540
Aren't you hungry?


00:27:41.795 --> 00:27:43.454
You can have it.


00:27:56.670 --> 00:27:58.744
You've got a damn good cook.


00:28:04.336 --> 00:28:05.495
- Hello!
- Here you go, sir.


00:28:08.545 --> 00:28:09.825
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.


00:28:21.503 --> 00:28:23.376
Look what came in the mail for you.


00:28:23.795 --> 00:28:25.665
- Prefect of police?
- Can I see?


00:28:30.670 --> 00:28:31.748
Oh, this?


00:28:34.295 --> 00:28:35.373
A week ago...


00:28:35.753 --> 00:28:36.749
as I was
coming home...


00:28:36.878 --> 00:28:38.584
I was walking past a church.


00:28:39.878 --> 00:28:43.659
When all of a sudden a man simply grabbed
my handbag and ran off.


00:28:43.920 --> 00:28:44.667
OhM God!


00:28:44.795 --> 00:28:45.328
Yeah.


00:28:46.461 --> 00:28:48.002
A horrible scar-faced man.


00:28:50.836 --> 00:28:53.835
It makes me shudder even now
to talk about it.


00:28:54.753 --> 00:28:55.831
I can imagine!


00:28:57.003 --> 00:28:58.081
You know what?


00:28:59.795 --> 00:29:02.367
I'll go down to the police station
and take care of it.


00:29:03.628 --> 00:29:05.785
Oh, no, no, don't bother with that.


00:29:07.378 --> 00:29:09.002
What are husbands for,
after all?!


00:29:11.628 --> 00:29:13.619
But really... Jacques!


00:29:14.461 --> 00:29:15.327
Jacques!


00:29:17.295 --> 00:29:20.874
How could you hit that tree
at two in the morning?


00:29:21.170 --> 00:29:24.535
You think if you have a fancy cabriolet
the whole town is yours?


00:29:25.045 --> 00:29:27.083
You could have killed your gal!


00:29:28.545 --> 00:29:31.496
I see in your file that you
were dead drunk!


00:29:32.836 --> 00:29:36.700
I don't understand... my wife...


00:29:38.545 --> 00:29:40.832
thief...


00:29:41.503 --> 00:29:43.376
her purse...


00:29:45.961 --> 00:29:48.829
Paul, come over, here is a guy...


00:29:49.920 --> 00:29:51.330
who cannot speak.


00:29:51.545 --> 00:29:53.916
No, not mute.
He only speaks English.


00:29:54.336 --> 00:29:55.747
Thank you.


00:30:01.920 --> 00:30:04.456
Good afternoon, sir.
How can I help you?


00:30:06.211 --> 00:30:08.582
Uhm, can you explain to him...


00:30:09.336 --> 00:30:11.576
My wife's purse has been stolen...


00:30:12.086 --> 00:30:14.836
and here is the summons.


00:30:17.336 --> 00:30:18.617
She told me that...


00:30:18.878 --> 00:30:21.284
Tell me, are you Mr. Ridolfi?


00:30:22.586 --> 00:30:23.285
No.


00:30:26.211 --> 00:30:28.534
What is this summons about?


00:30:29.336 --> 00:30:31.743
Apparently he's the little lady's husband.


00:30:33.170 --> 00:30:34.248
Shit...


00:30:34.920 --> 00:30:35.951
poor guy.


00:30:36.670 --> 00:30:37.950
What should we do?


00:30:38.128 --> 00:30:41.245
God, we must tell him,
this is the least we can do!


00:30:43.295 --> 00:30:45.417
Wait, I've got something for you.


00:30:58.961 --> 00:30:59.874
Here, you are...


00:31:03.461 --> 00:31:04.374
Jacques?


00:31:34.003 --> 00:31:35.330
I was at the
police station.


00:31:36.753 --> 00:31:37.619
Oh...


00:31:39.336 --> 00:31:40.498
I...


00:31:42.961 --> 00:31:44.206
They couldn't
find the file.


00:35:43.836 --> 00:35:45.211
How well you dance...


00:35:47.420 --> 00:35:49.410
You are full of suprises.


00:36:49.461 --> 00:36:50.576
Everything alright,
mates?


00:36:51.170 --> 00:36:51.999
Yes, sir!


00:36:57.045 --> 00:36:59.284
Isn't Fritzi the one on duty today?


00:36:59.628 --> 00:37:01.868
Yes, sir! But we traded shifts.


00:37:03.961 --> 00:37:06.580
Well, he wanted to see his son.


00:37:09.336 --> 00:37:10.877
The husband
is not home, sir...


00:37:14.920 --> 00:37:16.460
These husbands...


00:37:24.961 --> 00:37:26.502
It'll be blustery tonight.


00:37:27.086 --> 00:37:27.916
Aha...


00:37:46.545 --> 00:37:47.576
Habib...


00:37:47.878 --> 00:37:49.584
aren't you homesick sometimes?


00:37:50.711 --> 00:37:51.375
Well...


00:37:51.503 --> 00:37:52.960
For your wife for instance?


00:37:53.586 --> 00:37:55.210
You said you're married, right?


00:37:55.461 --> 00:37:57.915
Married, oh, yes, I'm married.
I have a wife.


00:37:58.753 --> 00:38:00.294
Young, beautiful one.


00:38:00.836 --> 00:38:02.377
Actually not one, two!


00:38:03.086 --> 00:38:04.034
Two?


00:38:04.670 --> 00:38:06.210
And an old one!


00:38:07.211 --> 00:38:10.625
We were brought up together.
She's the best, the fiercest!


00:38:14.378 --> 00:38:15.919
And what are they doing now?


00:38:18.170 --> 00:38:20.788
Three women without a man?
Aren't you a little worried?


00:38:20.920 --> 00:38:21.749
No!


00:38:22.545 --> 00:38:24.085
Come on, you can tell me.


00:38:24.503 --> 00:38:26.044
They're behind locked doors.


00:38:27.211 --> 00:38:28.752
My mother watches over them.


00:38:29.586 --> 00:38:31.826
My mother's still alive, she's 92!


00:38:36.920 --> 00:38:38.793
Don't they go stir-crazy?


00:38:39.795 --> 00:38:41.335
Maybe they do...


00:38:43.128 --> 00:38:44.669
but that's their problem,
not mine.


00:39:44.628 --> 00:39:45.659
Dedin!


00:39:49.295 --> 00:39:50.492
I didn't introduce you...


00:39:50.836 --> 00:39:52.211
but please
meet Jacques.


00:39:52.628 --> 00:39:54.999
Jacques, the husband of Lizzy.
And our Dedin.


00:39:56.086 --> 00:39:59.168
At last we get a chance
to meet the old sea-dog.


00:39:59.878 --> 00:40:02.450
I'm no more of a sea-dog
than you are a wharf rat.


00:40:04.295 --> 00:40:05.670
Am I right?


00:40:31.045 --> 00:40:32.621
What does the young man
do for a living?


00:40:32.920 --> 00:40:33.868
Oh, he's a writer.


00:40:36.753 --> 00:40:37.582
I mean...


00:40:37.753 --> 00:40:39.744
who are you speaking about?


00:40:41.003 --> 00:40:42.378
A writer...


00:40:48.295 --> 00:40:50.417
He also happens to have
a wealthy uncle.


00:40:53.295 --> 00:40:54.670
In other words,


00:40:55.128 --> 00:40:56.503
he's a parasite.


00:40:57.336 --> 00:40:59.126
You don't like him, do you?


00:41:02.753 --> 00:41:04.377
I saw that you didn't like him.


00:41:12.045 --> 00:41:13.751
But it would be
so nice if you did...


00:41:17.670 --> 00:41:18.618
Lizzy,


00:41:21.753 --> 00:41:24.041
you want me to like your admirer?


00:41:24.295 --> 00:41:25.670
He's not my admirer,


00:41:26.878 --> 00:41:28.253
you are completely insane!


00:41:28.461 --> 00:41:30.002
You can't fool me! Come on!


00:41:32.003 --> 00:41:33.378
You're just like
a brooding hen!


00:41:34.045 --> 00:41:35.420
Practically feverish!


00:41:36.503 --> 00:41:38.127
Are you comparing me to a hen?


00:41:39.170 --> 00:41:40.166
Yes, I am.


00:41:41.295 --> 00:41:43.168
And be glad
that's all it is, for now.


00:41:54.086 --> 00:41:55.461
How you have changed...


00:41:57.378 --> 00:41:59.084
You have really become so rude.


00:42:43.003 --> 00:42:45.243
Listen, Lizzy,


00:42:48.503 --> 00:42:49.878
after all,


00:42:50.753 --> 00:42:52.792
he is quiet a nice young man.


00:42:54.170 --> 00:42:55.035
We...


00:42:56.128 --> 00:42:58.960
We could invite him over,
if you want.


00:43:08.878 --> 00:43:11.663
I've got a job offer...


00:43:12.920 --> 00:43:16.285
to help out an old friend
who got seriously ill.


00:43:19.211 --> 00:43:21.250
It's a high-class pass anger ship.


00:43:22.336 --> 00:43:23.960
To Alexandria and back.


00:43:24.711 --> 00:43:26.086
Very posh.


00:43:28.211 --> 00:43:31.376
You know I don't like
those frail creatures...


00:43:31.628 --> 00:43:33.667
Somehow they make me anxious...


00:43:35.461 --> 00:43:36.374
but...


00:43:39.170 --> 00:43:40.959
Should I take the job?


00:43:44.545 --> 00:43:46.453
I can take you with me,
if you want.


00:43:50.836 --> 00:43:51.915
Ahem...


00:44:06.920 --> 00:44:07.998
Good morning!


00:44:16.128 --> 00:44:17.455
<i>Welcome aboard
the Marietta!</i>


00:44:17.670 --> 00:44:18.582
Thank you, sir!


00:44:19.711 --> 00:44:22.413
May I ask when Madame
is planning to arrive?


00:44:23.253 --> 00:44:26.252
We gave the captain's quarters
a bit more of a lady's touch.


00:44:26.920 --> 00:44:27.832
Actually,


00:44:29.128 --> 00:44:30.243
she's not coming.


00:44:31.045 --> 00:44:32.787
Oh, I'm sorry
to hear that.


00:44:33.586 --> 00:44:35.210
- I hope everything's fine.
- She's fine.


00:44:36.420 --> 00:44:37.960
Well, next time then perhaps.


00:44:39.336 --> 00:44:40.533
Let me show you around.


00:44:50.586 --> 00:44:51.961
Captain!


00:44:52.795 --> 00:44:54.917
Are you coming back to us after all?


00:44:55.878 --> 00:44:57.253
No, I'm sorry Tommy...


00:44:57.836 --> 00:45:00.586
Oh, yes, we've heard you've changed
for a more fancy job.


00:45:01.420 --> 00:45:03.209
It's just a one-time assignment.


00:45:04.336 --> 00:45:06.209
I only took it because of my wife.


00:45:06.836 --> 00:45:09.207
Oh, I see,
you bring her with you...


00:45:12.295 --> 00:45:14.452
Come on, let me buy you a drink!


00:45:14.878 --> 00:45:15.826
Great!


00:45:26.336 --> 00:45:27.617
Let's get a table inside!


00:45:40.086 --> 00:45:41.034
Thank you.


00:45:45.670 --> 00:45:47.792
Well, Tommy!
Tell me, what's new?


00:45:48.878 --> 00:45:50.454
Not much to tell...


00:45:50.586 --> 00:45:54.628
We'll set sail the day after tomorrow.
The captain is some Serbian fellow.


00:45:56.711 --> 00:45:57.790
Thank you.


00:46:00.961 --> 00:46:03.217
You have such a
handsome uniform, sir!


00:46:05.211 --> 00:46:06.871
<i>That Marietta!</i>


00:46:07.128 --> 00:46:08.538
She's a real looker!


00:46:09.836 --> 00:46:11.211
I went to see her...


00:46:11.836 --> 00:46:15.581
I mean, from the outside.
They wouldn't let me on board, so...


00:46:18.753 --> 00:46:20.661
Any news about Kodor?


00:46:21.753 --> 00:46:23.708
He is no longer around.


00:46:23.795 --> 00:46:25.170
He's big time now.


00:46:27.253 --> 00:46:27.952
How so?


00:46:31.128 --> 00:46:32.243
Last month...


00:46:32.545 --> 00:46:34.453
customs seized a large
shipment of cocaine.


00:46:35.170 --> 00:46:36.201
A major haul.


00:46:37.045 --> 00:46:38.918
They locked it up
in the customs depot.


00:46:39.920 --> 00:46:40.916
Next morning...


00:46:41.086 --> 00:46:42.710
the whole lot was burnt.


00:46:43.253 --> 00:46:44.249
But...


00:46:44.795 --> 00:46:46.833
Kodor had snuck
in the night before...


00:46:47.420 --> 00:46:49.245
and replaced it all with flour.


00:46:52.211 --> 00:46:53.243
Sweet!


00:46:55.253 --> 00:46:57.208
He became a real
big shot in Hamburg.


00:46:59.711 --> 00:47:00.790
I see!


00:47:44.211 --> 00:47:46.001
Captain! Fire! We are burning!


00:48:13.170 --> 00:48:14.876
Sir, should we
stop the engines?


00:48:15.170 --> 00:48:17.244
Perhaps, it is time to give
the SOS signals as well...


00:48:17.378 --> 00:48:20.950
Continue full steam, heading west
where we can catch the rain.


00:48:21.045 --> 00:48:24.418
We are going to burn, sir!
The deck is smouldering already!


00:48:25.336 --> 00:48:28.122
We can't risk waiting for a rescue boat!


00:48:29.128 --> 00:48:29.910
But!


00:48:30.420 --> 00:48:32.162
The rain will stop
the smouldering.


00:48:33.670 --> 00:48:34.831
Full steam, I said!


00:49:21.836 --> 00:49:22.749
Help me!


00:49:23.420 --> 00:49:24.332
Hey!


00:49:24.961 --> 00:49:26.040
Get him back inside!


00:49:28.795 --> 00:49:29.707
Stay here!


00:49:31.336 --> 00:49:32.581
Don't let anyone out!


00:50:03.461 --> 00:50:05.998
Shouldn't we send
the radio signals now, sir?


00:50:07.836 --> 00:50:08.749
We wait.


00:50:10.503 --> 00:50:11.748
It's going to rain.


00:50:17.753 --> 00:50:18.500
But...


00:50:18.878 --> 00:50:19.791
But what?


00:50:22.586 --> 00:50:24.826
Well, sir,
this is a delicate ship,


00:50:26.045 --> 00:50:27.870
with a fine, thin deck!


00:50:29.670 --> 00:50:31.708
It is not like some cargo ship.


00:50:32.836 --> 00:50:33.619
Sir...


00:51:20.420 --> 00:51:22.328
Guys, come quickly!


00:51:25.253 --> 00:51:27.161
Keep the pressure stable!


00:53:18.336 --> 00:53:19.249
Thank you.


00:53:21.878 --> 00:53:22.791
Don't you like it?


00:53:24.211 --> 00:53:25.871
I've switched to another kind.


00:53:29.961 --> 00:53:34.957
- What happened to your hand?
- We had a fire.


00:53:35.545 --> 00:53:36.126
Oh...


00:53:37.170 --> 00:53:38.912
Were you in any danger?


00:55:23.461 --> 00:55:24.374
Taxi!


00:55:33.753 --> 00:55:34.666
You are shivering.


00:55:34.961 --> 00:55:37.119
I'm so sorry
it's impossible to get a taxi...


00:55:37.545 --> 00:55:38.706
I don't feel very well.


00:55:39.461 --> 00:55:40.623
Poor darling.


00:55:42.461 --> 00:55:43.955
Well, I have a car.


00:55:44.920 --> 00:55:46.330
Should I bring you home?


00:55:48.128 --> 00:55:49.159
Come on, let's go.


00:55:49.711 --> 00:55:51.122
You are tired.


00:55:51.961 --> 00:55:53.288
You have to
get in your bed.


00:55:53.878 --> 00:55:56.659
- Thank you. That's very kind of you.
- You are welcome.


00:55:57.378 --> 00:55:59.168
Thank you very much,
it's so kind of you!


00:55:59.503 --> 00:56:00.618
My pleasure.


00:56:05.086 --> 00:56:06.959
Would you like to join me
for a tot of brandy?


00:56:07.420 --> 00:56:09.126
I've got a very special one
from Armenia.


00:56:09.420 --> 00:56:10.747
Oh, absolutely!


00:56:11.045 --> 00:56:12.290
With great pleasure!


00:56:13.170 --> 00:56:14.082
Jacques...


00:56:14.711 --> 00:56:15.541
please...


00:56:15.753 --> 00:56:16.666
We can go,
Maurice!


00:56:24.961 --> 00:56:25.874
This way?


00:56:26.211 --> 00:56:26.828
Yes.


00:56:31.503 --> 00:56:33.079
I'm gonna check on my wife.


00:56:59.753 --> 00:57:00.666
Here, your pills.


00:57:17.795 --> 00:57:19.454
I'm gonna put you to bed,
alright?


00:57:32.711 --> 00:57:34.418
What's the matter sweetheart?


00:57:55.336 --> 00:57:56.581
Please, don't...


00:58:00.503 --> 00:58:01.167
No...


00:58:05.961 --> 00:58:06.874
Don't...


00:58:17.461 --> 00:58:18.374
Stop it!


00:58:18.878 --> 00:58:19.577
Stop it!


00:58:20.253 --> 00:58:21.166
Please!


00:58:22.086 --> 00:58:22.620
Please!


00:58:22.795 --> 00:58:23.707
Stop it!


00:58:51.836 --> 00:58:52.749
So...


00:58:54.836 --> 00:58:56.784
- Nice car you have!
- Oh, thank you.


00:58:58.295 --> 00:58:59.705
Actually it's not mine.


00:59:00.378 --> 00:59:02.831
My uncle lands it to me
from time to time.


00:59:04.045 --> 00:59:06.119
So what do you do for a living?


00:59:07.253 --> 00:59:08.415
I do nothing.


00:59:09.378 --> 00:59:10.540
Well, now,


00:59:11.753 --> 00:59:12.998
that's a real answer.


00:59:14.711 --> 00:59:15.956
And what do you live on?


00:59:16.211 --> 00:59:18.534
Well, this is truely a mystery.


00:59:19.336 --> 00:59:21.161
Ah, so...


00:59:23.045 --> 00:59:24.211
it's a mistery...


00:59:24.253 --> 00:59:26.920
Listen captain, allow me
to give you a word of advice,


00:59:27.086 --> 00:59:29.919
as long as we are discussing
financial matters.


00:59:32.086 --> 00:59:32.999
Why?


00:59:34.086 --> 00:59:35.283
What do you know
about my life?


00:59:35.878 --> 00:59:38.628
And more to the point,
what business of yours is it?


00:59:41.378 --> 00:59:43.333
Let's not beat about the bush captain.


00:59:46.920 --> 00:59:47.832
Alright.


00:59:50.045 --> 00:59:51.704
I know very well
what a great shock


00:59:52.045 --> 00:59:54.035
that accident must have
been for you.


00:59:55.295 --> 00:59:57.369
Even if you chose not to talk about it.


00:59:58.420 --> 00:59:59.830
Everyone knows what a...


01:00:00.836 --> 01:00:03.325
"tour de force" it was
to save that ship.


01:00:10.628 --> 01:00:12.287
How do you know about that?


01:00:12.545 --> 01:00:14.583
Well I have certain naval connections.


01:00:16.128 --> 01:00:19.624
This specifically I heard
from Lord Cunningdale.


01:00:20.378 --> 01:00:21.919
He holds you in great esteem.


01:00:23.628 --> 01:00:24.457
You know him?


01:00:24.670 --> 01:00:25.333
Uhum.


01:00:25.670 --> 01:00:26.499
Really?


01:00:34.086 --> 01:00:35.413
Here, allow me!


01:00:38.378 --> 01:00:39.291
Thank you!


01:00:40.586 --> 01:00:41.499
Wait a minute!


01:00:42.211 --> 01:00:43.954
I promised you a drink.


01:00:45.711 --> 01:00:47.122
Shall we have a drop?


01:00:47.295 --> 01:00:48.207
But of course!


01:00:49.586 --> 01:00:53.035
You showed real mastery, resolving
that situation all by yourself.


01:00:53.795 --> 01:00:56.545
All those rescue services,
they skin you alive.


01:00:56.711 --> 01:00:58.833
But with good reason,
if you think about it.


01:00:59.836 --> 01:01:01.294
They employ only the best.


01:01:01.920 --> 01:01:02.785
It's only natural.


01:01:05.336 --> 01:01:07.576
And their ships always patrol
the most dangerous zones.


01:01:07.628 --> 01:01:08.494
Thank you.


01:01:11.378 --> 01:01:14.246
Actually, haven't you ever
thought of working for them?


01:01:15.795 --> 01:01:17.668
One of these rescue services?


01:01:17.878 --> 01:01:18.791
Why?


01:01:20.711 --> 01:01:22.122
That's a terrific idea!


01:01:24.545 --> 01:01:25.955
You are absolutely right!


01:01:28.795 --> 01:01:30.075
How did you ever
think of this?


01:01:30.378 --> 01:01:31.244
How not?


01:01:32.045 --> 01:01:33.455
The job needs courage,


01:01:33.670 --> 01:01:36.585
experience and the ability
to make quick decisions.


01:01:37.920 --> 01:01:39.994
Frankly, this is what
you're cut out for.


01:01:43.253 --> 01:01:45.244
Have you ever thought of
moving to Hamburg?


01:01:46.211 --> 01:01:48.202
Why Hamburg, of all places?


01:01:49.545 --> 01:01:51.418
Business is on the upswing there.


01:01:52.128 --> 01:01:53.373
You keep
hearing about it.


01:01:53.670 --> 01:01:54.582
True.


01:01:55.170 --> 01:01:56.248
I heard that too.


01:01:59.295 --> 01:02:00.207
But to move there?


01:02:00.878 --> 01:02:01.826
Why not?


01:02:03.836 --> 01:02:04.749
You know what?


01:02:06.086 --> 01:02:07.580
You're absolutely right.


01:02:08.086 --> 01:02:09.413
Nothing really
ties me here.


01:02:10.295 --> 01:02:12.250
I'm grateful for the idea!


01:02:12.670 --> 01:02:15.953
I wouldn't have thought you possesed
such a fine business sense.


01:02:16.336 --> 01:02:18.743
But only where it concerns others.


01:02:19.545 --> 01:02:21.998
For myself I don't manage
nearly as well,


01:02:22.336 --> 01:02:24.292
as you have been
good enough to observe.


01:02:24.836 --> 01:02:25.749
I...


01:02:26.461 --> 01:02:27.374
I didn't mean to...


01:02:27.711 --> 01:02:31.244
But it's a pleasure to be
of service to a real hero.


01:02:33.211 --> 01:02:34.871
The king of the ocean...


01:02:53.920 --> 01:02:57.831
I hope you had a pleasant time.


01:03:08.420 --> 01:03:09.332
Well...


01:03:33.170 --> 01:03:34.082
Good night.


01:03:56.045 --> 01:03:58.332
Captain! Is that you?


01:04:01.003 --> 01:04:01.620
How are you?


01:04:01.711 --> 01:04:03.169
I can't believe my eyes!


01:04:03.545 --> 01:04:05.535
You look so strange
without a uniform.


01:04:06.795 --> 01:04:08.419
You must be the captain's wife!


01:04:08.961 --> 01:04:10.704
God it must be exciting!


01:04:12.670 --> 01:04:13.618
Grete Winterhalter.


01:04:13.711 --> 01:04:14.624
Nice to meet you!


01:04:15.045 --> 01:04:16.290
I'll be right back.


01:04:49.753 --> 01:04:50.998
Isn't she sweet?


01:04:53.045 --> 01:04:54.455
She certainly is.


01:04:57.045 --> 01:04:59.996
She told me about the fire and
about everything else.


01:05:01.961 --> 01:05:04.083
I'm truly impressed!


01:05:09.170 --> 01:05:12.749
And if you plan to come home late,
please, let me know.


01:05:13.003 --> 01:05:15.409
I could offer you a spare key
to the front gate.


01:05:17.253 --> 01:05:18.996
And this key
is for your appartment.


01:05:20.878 --> 01:05:21.956
Welcome!


01:05:37.670 --> 01:05:39.246
What do you think?


01:05:39.586 --> 01:05:41.744
Could we change this furniture?


01:06:14.128 --> 01:06:15.538
Aren't you sleepy?


01:06:15.711 --> 01:06:16.624
No.


01:06:22.003 --> 01:06:23.746
Shall I tell you another story?


01:06:25.295 --> 01:06:26.207
Yes, please!


01:06:32.795 --> 01:06:35.580
Once there was a young man,


01:06:36.253 --> 01:06:39.583
who had been at sea since
the age of sixteen.


01:06:41.253 --> 01:06:45.117
Imprisoned aboard his ship
for months at a time.


01:06:47.711 --> 01:06:50.082
And yet, like any other young man...


01:06:51.086 --> 01:06:53.160
he madly yearned to be happy.


01:06:54.336 --> 01:06:56.955
Only he wasn't sure how to go about it.


01:06:58.045 --> 01:06:59.704
For his life had been...


01:06:59.920 --> 01:07:02.291
about something quite different,


01:07:04.295 --> 01:07:06.666
about duty and hard work.


01:07:08.253 --> 01:07:09.498
One day...


01:07:10.128 --> 01:07:13.079
his ship put in anchor on an island,


01:07:14.211 --> 01:07:15.954
the Island of Java.


01:07:18.045 --> 01:07:22.418
It was evening time and the young man
strolled among the tiny huts,


01:07:23.670 --> 01:07:25.412
alone in the cool night,


01:07:26.295 --> 01:07:28.037
among all these people...


01:07:29.586 --> 01:07:32.372
singing or laughing...


01:07:33.295 --> 01:07:37.455
or just chit-chatting in the depths
of their candle-lit huts.


01:07:39.753 --> 01:07:41.163
And he thought...


01:07:42.795 --> 01:07:44.205
he'd arrived...


01:07:44.753 --> 01:07:47.290
on the isle of the blessed.


01:07:51.128 --> 01:07:54.826
He would have liked to go
inside a hut, squat in a corner.


01:07:56.003 --> 01:07:58.456
He yearned so much
to be one of them...


01:07:59.961 --> 01:08:02.960
that his heart nearly
burst with longing.


01:08:05.003 --> 01:08:05.916
But...


01:08:08.211 --> 01:08:10.120
he didn't go inside any of the huts.


01:08:11.461 --> 01:08:13.037
And the next day...


01:08:13.628 --> 01:08:14.743
he sailed on.


01:08:25.170 --> 01:08:27.788
Why don't you tell me a story?


01:08:28.836 --> 01:08:29.749
Uhm...


01:08:30.961 --> 01:08:33.249
I'm not much good at telling stories.


01:08:41.003 --> 01:08:41.916
Come on...


01:08:43.878 --> 01:08:44.791
Just one!


01:08:45.253 --> 01:08:46.166
Please.


01:08:57.003 --> 01:08:57.916
You know...


01:08:59.295 --> 01:09:01.867
the rescue service will be
a fine job.


01:09:05.420 --> 01:09:06.700
I'll be away
a lot, but...


01:09:15.295 --> 01:09:16.492
Tell me the truth now.


01:09:17.920 --> 01:09:20.124
What pleasure do you find
in living with me?


01:09:28.128 --> 01:09:29.871
As God is my witness,


01:09:32.086 --> 01:09:34.623
I take great pleasure
in living with you.


01:09:36.253 --> 01:09:37.166
That girl...


01:09:38.295 --> 01:09:39.705
She's so beautiful.


01:09:42.461 --> 01:09:43.742
Why don't you marry her?


01:09:44.128 --> 01:09:45.408
Come on...


01:09:47.795 --> 01:09:50.461
You've nothing to fear
from that child.


01:09:50.628 --> 01:09:52.951
Young girls like her
never interested me at all.


01:09:53.170 --> 01:09:54.082
Don't touch me.


01:09:55.003 --> 01:09:56.330
Stop fooling Lizzy.


01:09:56.795 --> 01:09:58.750
There's nothing between
me and that girl.


01:09:59.211 --> 01:10:00.124
My God...


01:10:00.795 --> 01:10:02.703
Can't you see that I'm not jealous?


01:10:08.086 --> 01:10:09.497
What's got into you?


01:10:12.545 --> 01:10:14.832
Is it that young man? That Dedin?


01:10:15.920 --> 01:10:18.408
Well, as for him,
believe me he's a scoundrel.


01:10:21.170 --> 01:10:23.208
He wanted to whisk us
off to Hamburg.


01:10:23.378 --> 01:10:25.417
I'm just telling you so you know.


01:10:26.545 --> 01:10:28.287
He doesn't love you.


01:10:28.628 --> 01:10:29.375
Hey...


01:10:31.836 --> 01:10:32.749
Now...


01:10:37.503 --> 01:10:39.992
isn't it better to be
with the one who loves you?


01:10:41.295 --> 01:10:43.037
You think I don't love you.


01:10:44.545 --> 01:10:47.330
Yet you're still insisting
on keeping me.


01:10:50.545 --> 01:10:52.619
What kind of a man are you?


01:10:54.920 --> 01:10:56.828
Do you even have blood
in your veins?


01:11:01.711 --> 01:11:02.624
You know what?


01:11:05.920 --> 01:11:06.832
You're right.


01:11:10.711 --> 01:11:13.034
I don't know why
I'm still with you...


01:11:16.045 --> 01:11:19.458
and even if I crack my stupid
stubborn skull against the wall...


01:11:21.045 --> 01:11:24.992
I won't know the reason why I put up
with this humiliation.


01:11:26.086 --> 01:11:28.160
There's that girl,
who perhaps loves me.


01:11:28.753 --> 01:11:31.041
- That's what I'm trying to tell you.
- Don't talk!


01:11:31.378 --> 01:11:33.121
Don't breathe a word!


01:11:58.253 --> 01:12:00.825
It's a bit late for
an evening walk, isn't it?


01:12:02.461 --> 01:12:03.374
Excuse me?


01:12:03.545 --> 01:12:05.121
I'll close the door
in seven minutes.


01:12:05.378 --> 01:12:07.286
I don't like to be
woken up in the night!


01:12:07.878 --> 01:12:08.791
All right.


01:12:09.795 --> 01:12:12.911
That's fine, Mr... Herr Blume?


01:12:13.045 --> 01:12:13.957
Leopold Blume.


01:12:14.295 --> 01:12:17.791
By the way, you can have
full board, or just lunch?


01:12:18.503 --> 01:12:20.909
You forgot to tell me
when you rented the apartment.


01:12:22.836 --> 01:12:24.827
Ah... ah...


01:12:25.336 --> 01:12:27.494
Lunch... Lunch is fine.


01:12:28.170 --> 01:12:29.415
You're sure?


01:14:16.545 --> 01:14:17.920
We can divorce,


01:14:19.795 --> 01:14:21.122
if that's what you want.


01:14:27.670 --> 01:14:28.701
Can I say something?


01:14:30.503 --> 01:14:31.416
Say something.


01:14:32.711 --> 01:14:34.122
You are a big fool.


01:14:34.711 --> 01:14:35.624
There.


01:14:36.170 --> 01:14:37.415
Is that alright?


01:14:43.420 --> 01:14:44.913
And don't be cross with me.


01:14:56.295 --> 01:14:57.835
Ah, you're such a slob!


01:14:59.420 --> 01:15:00.332
Come here...


01:15:03.336 --> 01:15:04.912
Stop making a fool of me...


01:15:05.711 --> 01:15:06.624
And why?


01:15:07.503 --> 01:15:10.620
This is how the hero is welcomed back
by the home fireside.


01:15:11.878 --> 01:15:13.123
The fireside,


01:15:14.670 --> 01:15:15.831
in springtime?


01:15:17.711 --> 01:15:18.541
Come on,


01:15:18.670 --> 01:15:20.329
stop all that
huffing and puffing,


01:15:21.086 --> 01:15:22.746
the lover's role
is not right for you.


01:15:23.295 --> 01:15:23.876
Oh!


01:15:25.045 --> 01:15:25.708
And why?


01:15:29.003 --> 01:15:29.916
You're all set.


01:15:32.045 --> 01:15:33.290
You look handsome.


01:15:34.503 --> 01:15:35.451
Take a look
in the mirror.


01:15:35.753 --> 01:15:37.744
No, no.
I won't look in the mirror.


01:15:38.628 --> 01:15:40.204
So, tell me,


01:15:41.461 --> 01:15:44.910
why do you think
I'm unsuited for the lovers role?


01:15:48.045 --> 01:15:48.957
Well...


01:15:51.461 --> 01:15:53.251
Is a lovebird really like this?


01:15:53.836 --> 01:15:54.749
Why?


01:15:56.378 --> 01:15:58.168
What is a lovebird like?


01:15:59.378 --> 01:16:00.540
Insolent.


01:16:01.378 --> 01:16:02.540
What am I?


01:16:04.086 --> 01:16:05.331
You are honest.


01:16:06.211 --> 01:16:07.326
Don't say!


01:16:08.003 --> 01:16:09.876
Should I be a scoundrel?


01:16:13.086 --> 01:16:13.999
Well,


01:16:14.795 --> 01:16:15.707
a little bit...


01:16:18.045 --> 01:16:20.202
You don't have to be
so manly all the time!


01:16:23.128 --> 01:16:24.704
Full steam ahead!


01:16:26.503 --> 01:16:28.246
So you don't want
me to be manly.


01:16:28.878 --> 01:16:29.791
Fine.


01:16:31.086 --> 01:16:32.995
How would you like me to be?


01:16:34.295 --> 01:16:36.120
How should I know...


01:16:37.836 --> 01:16:40.373
act like you have ravaged
every virgin in sight...


01:16:41.295 --> 01:16:42.207
Get the picture?


01:16:42.878 --> 01:16:43.744
Hm...


01:16:52.336 --> 01:16:54.955
It's useless to wait for life
to accomodate you.


01:16:56.211 --> 01:16:57.787
You must accomodate life.


01:16:59.461 --> 01:17:01.417
Otherwise it will punish you.


01:17:07.961 --> 01:17:09.502
Now that I've trained you,


01:17:10.295 --> 01:17:12.285
you can go out
and flirt a little bit.


01:17:13.670 --> 01:17:14.831
But not too much.


01:17:34.878 --> 01:17:36.502
Tell me, what am I doing?


01:17:36.711 --> 01:17:38.122
Have I gone completely mad?


01:17:39.128 --> 01:17:41.368
I know a nice little hotel nearby.


01:17:47.670 --> 01:17:48.582
What?


01:17:52.086 --> 01:17:53.497
Look into my eyes.


01:17:55.170 --> 01:17:56.331
Do you really love me?


01:17:56.670 --> 01:17:57.582
I adore you!


01:17:58.753 --> 01:17:59.998
You don't love me.


01:18:01.878 --> 01:18:02.791
Hey!


01:18:03.586 --> 01:18:04.499
Grete!


01:18:05.545 --> 01:18:06.742
Don't be foolish!


01:18:10.920 --> 01:18:12.165
Where are you going?


01:18:15.128 --> 01:18:16.953
At least you're not lying.


01:18:18.503 --> 01:18:20.874
But this is important to me.


01:18:21.336 --> 01:18:22.368
For me as well...


01:18:34.253 --> 01:18:35.166
Look,


01:18:35.878 --> 01:18:36.791
wait here!


01:18:37.211 --> 01:18:39.534
I must pop into this hotel
on business.


01:18:40.086 --> 01:18:41.331
It's only for a minute.


01:18:43.961 --> 01:18:44.874
I love you.


01:18:48.211 --> 01:18:49.954
I won't! Don't even dream of it!


01:18:50.170 --> 01:18:51.082
Thank you!


01:18:58.503 --> 01:18:59.748
What took you so long?


01:19:01.295 --> 01:19:03.037
Didn't I tell you to hurry?


01:19:05.128 --> 01:19:07.332
You see, now it's too late.


01:19:09.336 --> 01:19:13.169
- What do you mean, it's too late?
- What do you mean, what do I mean?


01:19:13.545 --> 01:19:14.955
What were you thinking?


01:19:16.461 --> 01:19:19.033
You imagine all Hamburg
is waiting for your arrival?


01:19:21.420 --> 01:19:22.913
The job has been taken.


01:19:23.920 --> 01:19:24.749
I see.


01:19:25.086 --> 01:19:26.283
And anyway...


01:19:27.711 --> 01:19:29.205
What is this fancy jacket?


01:19:29.878 --> 01:19:32.663
How come you look
so smug and contented?


01:19:33.045 --> 01:19:35.119
It's the ladies, old man.


01:19:35.503 --> 01:19:38.075
It's the ladies.
You know how it is.


01:19:38.295 --> 01:19:39.409
Ah, yes...


01:19:40.128 --> 01:19:42.368
the ladies!


01:19:43.211 --> 01:19:45.748
Then it's alright.
These things happen.


01:19:46.836 --> 01:19:49.124
We'll come up with something.
No problem.


01:19:51.086 --> 01:19:53.042
And now off you go, I'm busy.


01:19:56.628 --> 01:19:57.541
Hey!


01:20:00.211 --> 01:20:01.326
Give me the number!


01:20:07.836 --> 01:20:11.534
Hello, so you took a look
at those documents?


01:20:13.253 --> 01:20:15.161
Look, I don't want to waste time...


01:20:26.920 --> 01:20:28.496
Oh, God...


01:20:35.670 --> 01:20:36.582
I'm so sorry,


01:20:36.920 --> 01:20:37.832
I'm so sorry!


01:20:41.170 --> 01:20:42.746
Did you get your business done?


01:20:43.295 --> 01:20:44.207
Yes.


01:20:45.170 --> 01:20:47.374
Let's go somewhere inside
and get ourselves dry.


01:20:49.461 --> 01:20:51.619
Don't be silly, I don't mean...


01:20:52.003 --> 01:20:54.042
I must go home,
my parents will worry.


01:20:56.253 --> 01:20:57.415
When will I see you?


01:20:58.461 --> 01:20:59.493
Ten in the morning?


01:20:59.711 --> 01:21:00.245
Ten o'clock?


01:21:01.420 --> 01:21:02.332
I can't wait.


01:21:04.003 --> 01:21:05.283
I'm so sorry.


01:25:55.711 --> 01:25:57.287
What a dreadful city.


01:26:01.211 --> 01:26:02.787
Why is it so dreadful?


01:26:06.045 --> 01:26:08.416
I fear this is where
I'll meet my end.


01:26:38.836 --> 01:26:40.626
I must go into town.


01:26:41.961 --> 01:26:43.372
I see Kodor at ten.


01:26:48.545 --> 01:26:49.623
Yes, of course,


01:26:50.336 --> 01:26:51.249
you must go...


01:27:00.128 --> 01:27:01.622
Although I wonder,


01:27:02.461 --> 01:27:04.204
what's the point? I mean...


01:27:04.878 --> 01:27:06.158
he only talks big.


01:27:16.795 --> 01:27:18.252
The hell with Kodor.


01:27:24.586 --> 01:27:25.748
I'm staying with you.


01:27:30.503 --> 01:27:31.416
Well...


01:27:32.753 --> 01:27:33.998
if that's
what you think...


01:27:41.920 --> 01:27:42.916
Hey,
listen to this!


01:27:44.461 --> 01:27:48.159
Two spinster cousins were living
together in a small town.


01:27:49.211 --> 01:27:51.618
The younger had grown
tired of the other one.


01:27:52.253 --> 01:27:53.829
She was in love, and...


01:27:54.711 --> 01:27:57.544
the other cousin
kept pestering her.


01:27:58.545 --> 01:28:00.169
So she poisoned her.


01:28:00.503 --> 01:28:01.534
With nicotine.


01:28:02.045 --> 01:28:02.827
Hmm...


01:28:05.045 --> 01:28:08.659
Can you really kill someone
with nicotine that easily?


01:28:09.253 --> 01:28:10.166
Yes.


01:28:10.878 --> 01:28:12.123
Quite easily.


01:28:16.461 --> 01:28:17.374
Poor thing.


01:28:19.003 --> 01:28:20.413
Yes, it's an ugly story.


01:28:21.086 --> 01:28:23.836
Just think. No one would
ever have found out,


01:28:24.670 --> 01:28:26.660
but this silly girl
let it slip by accident.


01:28:29.003 --> 01:28:30.497
But who are
you talking about?


01:28:31.795 --> 01:28:32.956
What do you mean who?


01:28:33.586 --> 01:28:35.162
Haven't you been listening?


01:28:37.920 --> 01:28:40.871
Your point of view is rather
interesting, don't you think?


01:28:41.711 --> 01:28:42.743
And why?


01:28:43.295 --> 01:28:45.582
At last she could
have enjoyed her life.


01:28:46.711 --> 01:28:48.086
In freedom.


01:28:51.170 --> 01:28:52.331
But Lizzy...


01:28:53.628 --> 01:28:55.702
you're talking about...


01:28:56.378 --> 01:28:58.950
Come on... You just
don't want to understand.


01:29:23.920 --> 01:29:24.916
You know what?


01:29:28.003 --> 01:29:30.374
I'd rather go and see
Kodor after all.


01:29:34.086 --> 01:29:34.999
Ah!


01:29:41.420 --> 01:29:42.249
What happened?


01:29:42.461 --> 01:29:43.374
My foot...


01:29:44.253 --> 01:29:45.710
I have a terrible cramp.


01:29:48.003 --> 01:29:48.916
Let me see it.


01:31:11.170 --> 01:31:12.118
You're alive!


01:31:18.336 --> 01:31:20.825
I dreamt of you last night,
and it was so terrible...


01:31:21.086 --> 01:31:23.125
I just sat by a window and
wept for you. And...


01:31:23.670 --> 01:31:25.625
then I arrived here,
I see this crowd,


01:31:26.211 --> 01:31:28.285
standing around a body,
and you're still not here...


01:31:29.711 --> 01:31:32.082
Oh, my God, I'm so sorry.


01:31:33.545 --> 01:31:34.457
Last night,


01:31:36.670 --> 01:31:38.376
when I woke up from
that dream,


01:31:38.878 --> 01:31:40.123
I just sat and sat,


01:31:40.420 --> 01:31:42.494
unable to fall asleep again.


01:31:44.045 --> 01:31:45.918
And I thought it over, and


01:31:49.420 --> 01:31:50.747
if you still want me to...


01:31:50.961 --> 01:31:53.332
I'll go... to a hotel with you.


01:32:23.170 --> 01:32:24.082
Don't...


01:32:46.045 --> 01:32:46.957
Hey...


01:32:48.045 --> 01:32:49.621
I love you so much...


01:32:50.461 --> 01:32:51.374
but...


01:32:52.920 --> 01:32:54.081
You're right.


01:32:58.045 --> 01:33:01.079
I just realized what a heartless
creature I've become.


01:33:03.253 --> 01:33:04.498
I wasn't always like this.


01:33:07.920 --> 01:33:08.832
It's just...


01:33:15.753 --> 01:33:16.666
Tell me,


01:33:20.170 --> 01:33:21.663
will you be my wife?


01:33:26.878 --> 01:33:27.707
Yes!


01:33:29.420 --> 01:33:30.581
Yes, I will.


01:33:32.003 --> 01:33:33.248
Do you really mean it?


01:33:33.711 --> 01:33:34.624
Believe me,


01:33:35.836 --> 01:33:38.622
I'd rather die than go on
the way I'm living now.


01:33:42.378 --> 01:33:43.623
Take me as your wife,


01:33:44.878 --> 01:33:46.205
but truly, marry me!


01:33:46.420 --> 01:33:48.410
I will show you what
a good wife I'll be...


01:34:09.211 --> 01:34:11.830
- Why are you cross now?
- Why would I be cross?


01:34:12.670 --> 01:34:13.915
I'm not angry!


01:34:16.336 --> 01:34:18.327
Anyway, it's not
my style to just get...


01:34:18.961 --> 01:34:20.419
cross with someone.


01:34:20.961 --> 01:34:22.952
I'm not one of your French hussies.


01:34:23.961 --> 01:34:24.411
Hey!


01:34:27.503 --> 01:34:28.665
Look here,


01:34:29.211 --> 01:34:32.293
you're obviously angry
with me because of my wife.


01:34:33.045 --> 01:34:34.455
That's really not fair.


01:34:39.336 --> 01:34:40.202
And anyway...


01:34:41.795 --> 01:34:43.170
why worry about her?


01:34:44.086 --> 01:34:46.705
Soon I'll be divorced.
I told you that.


01:34:51.211 --> 01:34:52.835
Ah... Divorce...


01:34:53.670 --> 01:34:55.792
It's never an easy thing.


01:34:57.586 --> 01:34:59.826
- Especially in such a case--
- Such as what?


01:35:03.086 --> 01:35:05.623
You'll never be able
to break away from her.


01:35:06.003 --> 01:35:07.709
No matter how much I love you.


01:35:09.545 --> 01:35:10.457
You know why?


01:35:12.128 --> 01:35:13.752
Because you're not like that.


01:35:14.295 --> 01:35:15.291
You're like me.


01:35:16.795 --> 01:35:18.371
You have a faithful heart.


01:36:42.420 --> 01:36:45.536
Right now we have a party to go to.


01:36:46.753 --> 01:36:48.910
I'm closing on
a fabulous deal, old man!


01:36:49.295 --> 01:36:51.783
They all think I'm doing them a favour.


01:36:52.045 --> 01:36:53.455
Can you believe that?


01:36:54.003 --> 01:36:54.371
Mhm.


01:36:55.920 --> 01:36:57.709
Come on now, out with it.


01:36:58.086 --> 01:36:59.503
What is the matter with you?


01:36:59.545 --> 01:37:01.085
I barely recognize you.


01:37:10.753 --> 01:37:12.128
What are you talking about?


01:37:14.461 --> 01:37:15.374
When?


01:37:15.961 --> 01:37:16.874
Back then.


01:37:17.628 --> 01:37:18.659
There, at the...


01:37:18.920 --> 01:37:19.702
Mhm.


01:37:22.420 --> 01:37:24.992
And did you really
marry the first woman...?


01:37:25.878 --> 01:37:26.956
Yes.


01:37:27.128 --> 01:37:28.622
How come you
never told me...?


01:37:31.711 --> 01:37:34.034
You've got more guts than I thought.


01:37:35.670 --> 01:37:37.329
Now let's get to business!


01:37:38.711 --> 01:37:40.750
Help me and I'll make you rich!


01:37:42.128 --> 01:37:43.041
Take it!


01:37:43.295 --> 01:37:44.575
Be flashy tonight.


01:37:46.336 --> 01:37:47.284
Look at him!


01:37:48.961 --> 01:37:50.621
My oldest friend,


01:37:51.378 --> 01:37:53.121
a real tough sea captain!


01:37:54.211 --> 01:37:56.913
He can swig a tumblerful
in a single gulp!


01:38:09.795 --> 01:38:11.501
Oh! Doesn't he have
an Adam's apple?


01:38:11.795 --> 01:38:12.992
Doesn't he have a soul?


01:38:22.503 --> 01:38:24.162
I intend to seduce you.


01:38:33.128 --> 01:38:34.455
Mr. Kodor,


01:38:35.211 --> 01:38:37.036
we would appreciate it if you...


01:38:37.253 --> 01:38:40.667
once again summed
up the terms for our benefit.


01:38:41.961 --> 01:38:44.794
Please, have some
consideration for the ladies...


01:38:45.295 --> 01:38:47.582
let's not talk about business tonight.


01:38:48.211 --> 01:38:49.871
I just wanted to say...


01:38:50.086 --> 01:38:51.497
My dear gentlemen!


01:38:52.878 --> 01:38:56.920
Let's not spoil this lovely
evening by talking business.


01:38:57.628 --> 01:39:01.243
After all, we have agreed on
everything. Isn't that so?


01:39:01.378 --> 01:39:03.128
In my opinion
a few points still remain...


01:39:03.170 --> 01:39:04.201
- Please...
- Doctor...


01:39:04.295 --> 01:39:05.373
Dear gentlemen!


01:39:05.586 --> 01:39:08.786
I drink to the success of
our consortium!


01:39:09.211 --> 01:39:10.243
Cheers!


01:39:42.836 --> 01:39:43.500
So...


01:39:44.795 --> 01:39:45.707
alright,


01:39:46.045 --> 01:39:48.368
sign it there and there...


01:39:49.586 --> 01:39:51.127
and we are done.


01:39:51.628 --> 01:39:54.330
I told you,
I'll make you rich!


01:39:57.753 --> 01:40:01.167
Kodor and Sons...
petrol consortium...


01:40:03.711 --> 01:40:04.878
I didn't know
you had sons!


01:40:04.920 --> 01:40:05.832
Well...


01:40:06.503 --> 01:40:07.913
Not that I know of,


01:40:08.378 --> 01:40:10.452
but it sound more classy this way.


01:40:10.836 --> 01:40:12.496
Don't you find?


01:40:13.586 --> 01:40:15.329
What is this, actually?


01:40:15.420 --> 01:40:18.086
What is it, what is it...
What do you care?


01:40:18.836 --> 01:40:20.211
You are just confirming


01:40:20.336 --> 01:40:23.501
that no one had objections to
the conditions of the deal.


01:40:26.378 --> 01:40:27.623
You know,


01:40:27.920 --> 01:40:30.456
I want to cheat these people.


01:40:31.211 --> 01:40:32.456
- Just a bit.
- But...


01:40:32.878 --> 01:40:34.833
Aren't these people
going to be bankrupt?


01:40:34.920 --> 01:40:37.919
And why should't they?
What a story!


01:40:38.628 --> 01:40:41.496
So what are you?
A virgin?


01:40:43.128 --> 01:40:45.996
Just say you do not want
to sign and that's that.


01:40:49.586 --> 01:40:50.665
Alright.


01:40:53.461 --> 01:40:53.876
Bravo.


01:41:22.961 --> 01:41:24.786
Tell me your honest opinion,


01:41:25.753 --> 01:41:28.704
do you believe in
a higher intelligence?


01:41:30.128 --> 01:41:31.408
A higher?


01:41:33.170 --> 01:41:34.628
What the hell
are you talking about?


01:41:34.670 --> 01:41:35.417
But...


01:41:35.711 --> 01:41:38.710
Don't you believe in the movement
of the stars, in a cosmic order?


01:41:42.836 --> 01:41:45.787
Why must your kind
always bring up the stars!


01:41:46.336 --> 01:41:47.711
Why not a carrot?


01:41:48.086 --> 01:41:49.283
A carrot?


01:41:49.795 --> 01:41:52.413
It's a miracle of nature
as much as a star!


01:41:59.586 --> 01:42:00.250
Hello!


01:42:00.420 --> 01:42:02.162
You are so sweet
when you're drunk!


01:42:03.336 --> 01:42:04.830
Anyhow,


01:42:05.836 --> 01:42:11.454
these two millionaire heiresses
I ran into at Kodor's...


01:42:12.795 --> 01:42:17.749
One was like a vanilla cake,
and the other one


01:42:18.253 --> 01:42:20.706
had a waist like a violin...


01:42:21.920 --> 01:42:23.496
You're such a poet!


01:42:25.503 --> 01:42:26.913
Both of them,


01:42:29.253 --> 01:42:30.663
I swear to you...


01:42:31.295 --> 01:42:32.705
proposed to me...


01:42:33.336 --> 01:42:36.287
But how can I marry two of them
at the same time?


01:42:37.378 --> 01:42:40.045
Didn't you let them know that
you already have a wife?


01:42:40.253 --> 01:42:43.252
Of course I did!
They couldn't care less!


01:42:45.420 --> 01:42:46.332
It's funny.


01:42:47.753 --> 01:42:50.704
Only yesterday someone
proposed to me as well.


01:42:55.670 --> 01:42:57.127
Would you let me go?


01:43:03.503 --> 01:43:07.331
Sir, if you hire me
to gather evidence for divorce,


01:43:08.003 --> 01:43:10.042
to catch the parties in flagrante,


01:43:10.461 --> 01:43:12.286
that would be quite
a different rate...


01:43:12.670 --> 01:43:17.043
than if you just want me to provide
a list of where, with whom,


01:43:17.545 --> 01:43:20.211
and how many times Madame
is doing it.


01:43:20.670 --> 01:43:21.333
Now...


01:43:23.878 --> 01:43:26.959
if you also need the intimate details,


01:43:27.461 --> 01:43:31.159
positions, accessories used in the act...


01:43:31.503 --> 01:43:32.332
But...


01:43:34.128 --> 01:43:36.499
I am not at all sure that
there is actually an act!


01:43:42.711 --> 01:43:44.501
And do you really
want to know?


01:43:45.753 --> 01:43:47.792
Sometimes it is better not to.


01:43:47.920 --> 01:43:50.326
I simply would like to know
what she does all day.


01:43:50.545 --> 01:43:51.955
Let me tell you something.


01:43:53.086 --> 01:43:54.959
I have been doing it
for thirty years.


01:43:55.420 --> 01:43:58.419
Trailing women has given me
flat feet and rheumatism.


01:43:59.629 --> 01:44:02.580
You will never believe
what they are capable of.


01:44:03.836 --> 01:44:05.994
In my experience, dear sir,


01:44:06.753 --> 01:44:09.455
there is no such thing
as an innocent woman.


01:44:12.253 --> 01:44:13.119
Jacques?


01:44:17.378 --> 01:44:17.995
Yes?


01:44:18.128 --> 01:44:19.704
Would you
button me up, please?


01:44:29.878 --> 01:44:31.786
Lizzy, tell me sincerely,


01:44:32.836 --> 01:44:34.792
who proposed to you
the other day?


01:44:38.629 --> 01:44:40.620
What a big ninny you are!


01:44:42.045 --> 01:44:43.538
I can't believe
you took me seriously,


01:44:45.378 --> 01:44:46.919
I really can't believe it!


01:45:23.836 --> 01:45:25.211
A quarter pound
of flour, please.


01:45:25.461 --> 01:45:27.251
May I know
what you need it for?


01:45:27.711 --> 01:45:29.287
What... why?


01:45:30.296 --> 01:45:33.626
I'd like some flour.
Easy enough, isn't it?


01:45:33.711 --> 01:45:36.082
Sir, we have nine
different types of flour.


01:45:36.253 --> 01:45:37.912
Is it for leavened dough
or for puff-pastry?


01:45:38.211 --> 01:45:40.120
Or perhaps for cooking?


01:45:40.711 --> 01:45:41.790
That's it, cooking.


01:45:51.296 --> 01:45:52.327
Hey!


01:45:53.211 --> 01:45:54.373
Hey sweetheart!


01:45:54.878 --> 01:45:55.577
Uhm...


01:45:57.378 --> 01:46:01.123
Did I tell you that
I'm going to Bruges this evening?


01:46:02.045 --> 01:46:03.585
Uhm... Yes!


01:46:05.962 --> 01:46:08.369
Kodor finally came through... yes...


01:46:09.586 --> 01:46:10.452
Uhm...


01:46:10.795 --> 01:46:13.367
I'll be gone for two days.
So uhm...


01:46:14.420 --> 01:46:15.451
See you in two days!


01:46:15.836 --> 01:46:16.334
Bye!


01:46:16.920 --> 01:46:17.418
Bye!


01:47:07.336 --> 01:47:08.498
Haven't you set out?


01:47:10.920 --> 01:47:12.247
The trip was canceled.


01:47:35.753 --> 01:47:36.749
Who's that?


01:47:43.378 --> 01:47:44.623
Don't, please,
don't go!


01:47:45.170 --> 01:47:45.999
Why shouldn't I?


01:47:46.253 --> 01:47:47.166
Don't leave me alone!


01:48:24.878 --> 01:48:26.372
Do you know who
knocked on our door?


01:48:27.003 --> 01:48:27.869
Did you seen him?


01:48:29.253 --> 01:48:30.082
I did.


01:48:30.836 --> 01:48:31.666
So?


01:48:32.086 --> 01:48:32.916
It was me.


01:48:34.629 --> 01:48:35.376
Oh...


01:48:36.878 --> 01:48:38.372
And why,
if I may ask?


01:48:39.336 --> 01:48:42.122
Well, you took the front gate key
and didn't give it back.


01:48:43.670 --> 01:48:44.499
Oh...


01:48:45.586 --> 01:48:46.582
You're right!


01:48:50.878 --> 01:48:53.331
And why do you need that lousy key
at the crack of dawn?


01:48:54.878 --> 01:48:55.826
It's Friday!


01:48:55.962 --> 01:48:56.958
So what?


01:48:58.170 --> 01:49:00.078
I have to go to the market.


01:49:00.962 --> 01:49:02.077
I'm late already.


01:49:02.253 --> 01:49:05.204
They'll make me pay double
for everything, those robbers.


01:49:07.545 --> 01:49:09.121
What's this mess here'?


01:49:10.753 --> 01:49:12.329
What do you keep
in your pockets?


01:49:12.420 --> 01:49:13.534
What do you mean?


01:49:14.629 --> 01:49:15.660
This...


01:49:16.670 --> 01:49:17.784
That... Uhm...


01:49:21.795 --> 01:49:23.501
I'll let you guess what it is.


01:49:35.086 --> 01:49:36.082
It's uhm...


01:49:39.962 --> 01:49:41.373
It's a bit of cocaine.


01:49:43.003 --> 01:49:44.746
And what do you need cocaine for?


01:49:45.378 --> 01:49:46.244
Dear God...


01:49:46.503 --> 01:49:49.205
I also need something
to make my life more bearable.


01:49:53.545 --> 01:49:55.453
It's a bit of flour, it really is.


01:49:58.836 --> 01:50:00.579
I wanted to sprinkle it
on the threshold


01:50:00.795 --> 01:50:02.869
to find out who
climbs into our bed


01:50:02.962 --> 01:50:04.077
when I'm not home.


01:50:21.211 --> 01:50:23.878
Most peculiar...


01:50:26.003 --> 01:50:27.165
The point is...


01:50:28.296 --> 01:50:30.418
your wife seems
to be faithful to you.


01:50:31.795 --> 01:50:33.205
She's a charming creature.


01:50:33.962 --> 01:50:35.586
I can only congratulate you.


01:50:40.128 --> 01:50:44.335
But, you know, I can continue
for half price for one more month,


01:50:45.128 --> 01:50:47.167
lovers can have
longer absences, you know.


01:50:47.253 --> 01:50:49.576
Just give me the bill
and we call this off.


01:50:56.711 --> 01:50:57.992
They're beautiful!


01:51:04.296 --> 01:51:05.292
Here you are.


01:51:05.545 --> 01:51:06.327
Thank you!


01:51:09.753 --> 01:51:11.661
You're turning into quite a gentleman!


01:51:13.420 --> 01:51:15.743
You know that this is the first time
you buy me flowers?


01:51:19.920 --> 01:51:21.544
I'll fill the vase with water.


01:52:07.336 --> 01:52:08.332
Nice!


01:52:10.003 --> 01:52:10.999
Are you alright?


01:52:13.003 --> 01:52:14.662
You look like death...


01:52:23.420 --> 01:52:24.285
Captain!


01:52:25.503 --> 01:52:26.499
What an ho nor!


01:52:27.296 --> 01:52:29.204
Your reputation precedes you!


01:52:30.170 --> 01:52:30.999
A cigar?


01:52:31.503 --> 01:52:32.783
I'm fine, thank you!


01:52:33.962 --> 01:52:35.243
But enough chatter...


01:52:35.545 --> 01:52:37.287
How can I be of service to you?


01:52:39.003 --> 01:52:40.579
I'll get straight to the point.


01:52:41.920 --> 01:52:42.832
I need work.


01:52:44.545 --> 01:52:45.374
How come...


01:52:47.211 --> 01:52:50.044
But, sure, sure,
it is a real ho nor you chose us!


01:52:51.296 --> 01:52:53.453
Well, the Yasmin a
is leaving for Cape Town.


01:52:53.545 --> 01:52:55.370
Carrying English broadcloth.


01:52:56.045 --> 01:52:58.167
I can move the captain
to another ship...


01:52:58.253 --> 01:52:59.710
you take his place.


01:52:59.920 --> 01:53:01.875
No, the thing is...


01:53:02.711 --> 01:53:04.869
I have to find some work on dry land.


01:53:06.170 --> 01:53:09.370
Oh... I see. I'm truly sorry.


01:53:10.586 --> 01:53:11.961
Illness in the family?


01:53:12.336 --> 01:53:13.663
Something like that...


01:53:16.003 --> 01:53:16.702
Fred!


01:53:22.545 --> 01:53:24.868
Captain Störr has personal problems.


01:53:25.296 --> 01:53:27.286
Do we have any work for him?


01:53:28.253 --> 01:53:29.415
Please,
follow me, sir.


01:53:48.586 --> 01:53:49.831
You're still up,
working?


01:54:06.711 --> 01:54:07.790
Oh, my God.


01:54:08.586 --> 01:54:10.127
You should see your eyes.


01:54:11.128 --> 01:54:11.957
Why?


01:54:12.711 --> 01:54:14.038
What do they look like?


01:54:16.795 --> 01:54:17.791
They are so...


01:54:21.336 --> 01:54:22.368
beady.


01:54:26.420 --> 01:54:27.830
Are you angry at me?


01:54:43.211 --> 01:54:46.328
I have certainly painted
the town red tonight...


01:54:47.920 --> 01:54:49.034
I drank champagne...


01:54:49.878 --> 01:54:51.751
I even had some port,


01:54:52.128 --> 01:54:53.290
If you want to know...


01:54:54.128 --> 01:54:54.910
Mhm.


01:54:55.128 --> 01:54:55.957
Mhm.


01:54:57.253 --> 01:54:58.580
So I'm a bit tipsy.


01:55:01.170 --> 01:55:02.627
Do you have any idea how good


01:55:02.795 --> 01:55:05.118
cigarette smoke and chocolate
taste together?


01:55:06.878 --> 01:55:08.537
I learned that from a young man...


01:55:09.670 --> 01:55:10.499
tonight.


01:55:12.003 --> 01:55:13.283
Would you like to try it?


01:55:15.629 --> 01:55:17.123
I kept one for you.


01:55:19.753 --> 01:55:20.749
Together...


01:55:27.253 --> 01:55:28.331
I'll leave it here.


01:55:31.962 --> 01:55:33.207
I'm going to bed.


01:55:40.211 --> 01:55:41.243
Would you like to join?


01:57:17.920 --> 01:57:19.828
You're at work early today...


01:57:44.336 --> 01:57:45.332
What is it for?


01:57:46.045 --> 01:57:47.953
What do you mean, what is it for?


01:57:48.378 --> 01:57:49.374
That's right,


01:57:50.086 --> 01:57:52.077
I asked you what you need money for.


01:57:55.045 --> 01:57:56.953
I'm having lunch in town today...


01:57:59.045 --> 01:58:00.669
anyway, I have my expenses...


01:58:03.545 --> 01:58:05.038
Why don't you eat
lunch at home?


01:58:06.086 --> 01:58:07.497
Our meals are paid for.


01:58:07.795 --> 01:58:10.461
That indeed is a most
important consideration.


01:58:10.836 --> 01:58:13.076
Money isn't actually
pouring in at the moment.


01:58:13.336 --> 01:58:14.830
In case you haven't noticed.


01:58:17.670 --> 01:58:18.666
Well...


01:58:20.336 --> 01:58:21.498
If you say so...


01:58:53.586 --> 01:58:54.831
Ooops!


02:00:57.378 --> 02:00:58.705
Have you had your fun?


02:01:05.128 --> 02:01:06.076
What a clown...


02:01:34.461 --> 02:01:36.500
This is the menu of the next week.


02:01:36.962 --> 02:01:38.918
If there is anything you don't like,


02:01:39.378 --> 02:01:42.201
- perhaps I can make some changes.
- All right, fine, thank you!


02:01:42.336 --> 02:01:45.252
No, no, no, I read it out to you,
I don't have a copy!


02:01:48.296 --> 02:01:49.671
I'll come down later.


02:01:50.629 --> 02:01:51.707
At the moment...


02:01:51.920 --> 02:01:54.124
Actually I didn't really
come up for the menu...


02:01:54.711 --> 02:01:58.409
but in order to clear up
something about the carrots...


02:02:00.670 --> 02:02:01.499
The what?


02:02:02.170 --> 02:02:03.995
The... how do you say...


02:02:04.211 --> 02:02:06.451
the eternal soul of a carrot.


02:02:06.836 --> 02:02:08.460
Or of a cucumber.


02:02:08.920 --> 02:02:10.709
Or a pipe...


02:02:11.461 --> 02:02:14.033
I don't need to explain
to you your own idea.


02:02:14.253 --> 02:02:16.292
Listen, my wife isn't feeling well...


02:02:16.461 --> 02:02:18.002
Oh, why didn't you say so!


02:02:18.836 --> 02:02:21.373
She's not expecting
something little, is she?


02:02:21.836 --> 02:02:23.330
No, for God's sake!


02:02:24.420 --> 02:02:25.581
Excuse me...


02:03:35.086 --> 02:03:36.461
Finished, already.


02:03:36.878 --> 02:03:38.253
You're always on time.


02:03:41.253 --> 02:03:42.628
What happened
to these files?


02:03:43.503 --> 02:03:44.416
I'm sorry.


02:03:45.170 --> 02:03:46.035
Well,


02:03:46.461 --> 02:03:48.535
don't worry,
everything is visible, and,


02:03:49.170 --> 02:03:53.163
as much as I know you I'm sure,
it is flawlessy correct, as always.


02:03:53.920 --> 02:03:56.787
Fine, your pay is due next week.


02:04:02.128 --> 02:04:03.503
The thing is...


02:04:05.503 --> 02:04:06.878
could I get paid today?


02:04:11.503 --> 02:04:13.127
No, I'm afraid not.


02:04:13.253 --> 02:04:14.877
Check back here in three days.


02:04:32.586 --> 02:04:33.961
Good evening.
One bag, please.


02:04:34.336 --> 02:04:35.451
With pleasure!


02:04:36.711 --> 02:04:38.205
50 cents.


02:04:45.711 --> 02:04:47.086
That's fine...


02:04:48.962 --> 02:04:51.167
- Thank you!
- Have a nice evening!


02:07:09.253 --> 02:07:12.370
Let's hope you don't get pneumonia...


02:07:13.045 --> 02:07:14.325
Thank you.


02:07:15.503 --> 02:07:18.502
So... All this story you told me...


02:07:19.920 --> 02:07:21.460
How do you feel about it now?


02:07:23.545 --> 02:07:25.418
It's just miserable.


02:07:26.753 --> 02:07:27.619
Why?


02:07:28.128 --> 02:07:29.041
Why?


02:07:30.920 --> 02:07:33.408
I cannot even drown myself properly.


02:07:35.670 --> 02:07:37.459
That's a good one.


02:07:38.461 --> 02:07:39.836
No, but really,


02:07:40.420 --> 02:07:41.498
tell me!


02:07:42.629 --> 02:07:43.660
You tell me!


02:07:46.253 --> 02:07:48.126
Tell me, why can't I create some...


02:07:48.296 --> 02:07:50.500
order in my miserable little life?


02:07:52.795 --> 02:07:54.122
Well,


02:07:55.003 --> 02:07:55.999
who can...?


02:07:57.420 --> 02:07:59.458
Apparently, almost everyone.


02:08:05.170 --> 02:08:06.710
Have you ever seen a piglet?


02:08:08.086 --> 02:08:09.118
What?


02:08:09.586 --> 02:08:11.127
A soft little creature.


02:08:11.878 --> 02:08:15.920
It starts to squeal when grabbed
by strangers who want to eat it.


02:08:16.920 --> 02:08:19.705
Well, that's our lot on Earth,
more or less.


02:08:20.920 --> 02:08:24.001
We squeal or not...
doesn't matter much.


02:08:25.461 --> 02:08:27.998
Believe me, this world
is not made for us.


02:08:29.920 --> 02:08:32.670
It's not made for our soul.


02:08:34.586 --> 02:08:36.210
This is not it's home.


02:08:37.503 --> 02:08:39.542
So, don't be surprised.


02:08:43.420 --> 02:08:45.826
Do you realize how lucky you are?


02:08:46.836 --> 02:08:49.835
You can simply get up and...


02:08:50.545 --> 02:08:53.033
and leave all this misery behind!


02:08:55.795 --> 02:08:57.335
It just doesn't work.


02:08:58.711 --> 02:08:59.790
So what?


02:08:59.878 --> 02:09:00.909
Yeah, you're
right. But...


02:09:01.045 --> 02:09:03.711
I, for one, would do it
if I were in your place.


02:09:05.378 --> 02:09:06.919
I would do it.


02:09:08.795 --> 02:09:10.750
I imagine...


02:09:11.378 --> 02:09:12.919
I'm already dead...


02:09:13.503 --> 02:09:15.246
But before I die... I...


02:09:16.629 --> 02:09:18.917
I revive for one last time, and...


02:09:19.962 --> 02:09:21.503
and run away.


02:09:24.003 --> 02:09:24.951
I...


02:09:25.253 --> 02:09:27.043
I receive a brief reprieve,


02:09:28.296 --> 02:09:29.576
somewhere,


02:09:30.545 --> 02:09:33.117
a stranger cast up on
a strange shore.


02:09:34.920 --> 02:09:36.034
And...


02:09:38.336 --> 02:09:41.204
and isn't that what...
what life's all about?


02:09:43.170 --> 02:09:46.535
Receiving one reprieve after another?


02:10:42.711 --> 02:10:43.659
Jacques!


02:10:46.711 --> 02:10:48.454
Hey there my big captain!


02:10:50.670 --> 02:10:51.618
Come with me.


02:10:52.003 --> 02:10:53.994
I'm on my way to a punch party.


02:10:55.795 --> 02:10:56.660
Well...


02:11:04.336 --> 02:11:06.327
How about spending a night
on the town instead?


02:11:06.545 --> 02:11:07.742
There's an idea!


02:11:08.795 --> 02:11:10.252
I can't attend tonight.


02:11:13.336 --> 02:11:14.960
Please, apologize on my behalf,


02:11:15.753 --> 02:11:16.831
say I've got a cold,


02:11:19.086 --> 02:11:20.082
Guess what...?


02:11:20.753 --> 02:11:22.294
I met someone!


02:11:24.045 --> 02:11:24.993
He's...


02:11:26.629 --> 02:11:27.826
He's handsome,


02:11:28.211 --> 02:11:29.752
actually very handsome.


02:11:31.003 --> 02:11:32.200
He's got blue eyes,


02:11:32.920 --> 02:11:33.916
blonde hair,


02:11:34.586 --> 02:11:35.701
broad shoulders...


02:11:37.378 --> 02:11:38.291
He has this...


02:11:38.836 --> 02:11:40.247
special something...


02:11:45.753 --> 02:11:46.950
Well, I see
you tomorrow...


02:11:52.920 --> 02:11:54.247
Jacques?


02:12:01.128 --> 02:12:01.957
Madame!


02:12:03.086 --> 02:12:03.952
Madame!


02:12:04.296 --> 02:12:05.623
May I accompany you?


02:12:06.962 --> 02:12:09.416
I simply offer
a brief companionship.


02:12:12.420 --> 02:12:13.747
Brief and passing.


02:12:15.420 --> 02:12:18.170
After all, people get acquainted
in dance halls nowadays.


02:12:18.711 --> 02:12:20.702
Then may I suggest you
try a dancehall.


02:12:21.211 --> 02:12:22.408
Oh, please
have a heart.


02:12:23.545 --> 02:12:25.085
Soon enough
I'll be gone forever,


02:12:25.586 --> 02:12:27.246
far away,
to the end of the world...


02:12:28.586 --> 02:12:29.867
You see I'm a sailor,


02:12:30.545 --> 02:12:31.742
the captain of a ship.


02:12:33.962 --> 02:12:35.337
But are you
really a captain?


02:12:37.629 --> 02:12:39.223
Because you don't
look like one.


02:12:40.753 --> 02:12:41.919
I don't look like one?


02:12:43.629 --> 02:12:45.488
I've been here perhaps too long.


02:12:47.003 --> 02:12:49.525
Whew, if you only knew what
I've gone through in this city...


02:12:49.629 --> 02:12:50.542
Such as what?


02:12:50.711 --> 02:12:53.283
Tell me, I'd really like to hear this.


02:12:54.045 --> 02:12:56.119
My heart is so restless
my dear Madame,


02:12:56.211 --> 02:12:57.871
I have a broken heart!


02:12:58.086 --> 02:12:59.793
You're forgetting
one thing, sir.


02:13:00.461 --> 02:13:01.788
And that is?


02:13:03.378 --> 02:13:06.708
I happen to have a husband
whom I deeply love.


02:13:09.795 --> 02:13:11.040
You love your husband?


02:13:14.378 --> 02:13:15.788
What's so amazing
about that?


02:13:17.253 --> 02:13:18.082
My God...


02:13:19.920 --> 02:13:21.579
what kind of husband could he be?


02:13:22.336 --> 02:13:23.249
What kind?


02:13:23.920 --> 02:13:25.413
Well he's very nice.


02:13:26.086 --> 02:13:28.042
But what I think is even
more important,


02:13:28.878 --> 02:13:30.040
he's an honest man.


02:13:32.545 --> 02:13:33.374
Damn...


02:13:34.836 --> 02:13:36.496
a husband without a single fault?


02:13:37.586 --> 02:13:38.250
Well...


02:13:39.045 --> 02:13:40.290
he does have one.


02:13:41.545 --> 02:13:42.790
He does have one.


02:13:43.128 --> 02:13:44.373
He worries too much.


02:13:49.420 --> 02:13:52.086
Why, you, for example...


02:13:59.378 --> 02:14:00.788
are you faithful to him?


02:14:05.045 --> 02:14:06.455
What a laughable question...


02:14:07.962 --> 02:14:09.420
So charmingly stupid.


02:14:11.795 --> 02:14:13.288
Of course I'm
faithful to him!


02:14:14.296 --> 02:14:15.872
Didn't you know,
my dear Captain?


02:14:17.086 --> 02:14:18.710
If you really are a captain...


02:14:21.545 --> 02:14:22.410
Well...


02:14:24.586 --> 02:14:25.452
then...


02:14:27.629 --> 02:14:29.170
Come on,
you big silly thing.


02:14:30.045 --> 02:14:31.669
You proposed to
take me somewhere.


02:14:32.629 --> 02:14:34.040
My hands are getting cold.


02:16:48.253 --> 02:16:49.284
Be careful!


02:17:06.211 --> 02:17:07.586
You see,
you never courted me.


02:17:14.503 --> 02:17:15.748
Courted you?


02:17:16.836 --> 02:17:17.535
Yes...


02:17:18.586 --> 02:17:20.210
courting is a must.


02:17:25.962 --> 02:17:28.202
You know I could have died for you,


02:17:28.753 --> 02:17:30.033
I loved you so much.


02:17:33.795 --> 02:17:34.992
And that's over now?


02:17:36.753 --> 02:17:37.582
Yes.


02:17:38.461 --> 02:17:39.658
It's over now.


02:17:44.795 --> 02:17:46.122
What a pity.


02:17:51.545 --> 02:17:52.410
Yes.


02:17:55.836 --> 02:17:56.868
A pity...


02:17:58.670 --> 02:17:59.701
Or maybe not.


02:18:02.045 --> 02:18:03.918
Perhaps it was too much.


02:18:27.211 --> 02:18:28.243
Oh...


02:18:32.670 --> 02:18:33.701
You're feverish...


02:18:35.878 --> 02:18:37.253
Your head is burning up!


02:19:05.378 --> 02:19:06.409
Get well!


02:19:07.086 --> 02:19:08.118
Please get well!


02:19:09.211 --> 02:19:11.202
You'll see, I'll behave myself.


02:19:33.920 --> 02:19:35.117
What day is it?


02:19:35.836 --> 02:19:36.666
Wednesday.


02:19:41.211 --> 02:19:43.451
So I was ill for only two days...


02:19:44.629 --> 02:19:45.956
Somehow it seemed longer.


02:19:46.253 --> 02:19:47.628
It was indeed.


02:19:48.420 --> 02:19:49.795
It's already April,
my dear.


02:19:51.461 --> 02:19:52.078
Oh...


02:19:59.211 --> 02:20:00.752
How pale you are?


02:20:02.753 --> 02:20:04.294
What have we been living on?


02:20:04.586 --> 02:20:06.127
I sold some of my jewelry.


02:20:08.545 --> 02:20:10.085
It was difficult, wasn't it?


02:20:11.211 --> 02:20:11.958
It was.


02:20:12.962 --> 02:20:13.994
But it was beautiful.


02:20:17.503 --> 02:20:19.044
This came a little while ago.


02:20:23.753 --> 02:20:24.784
What is it?


02:20:30.336 --> 02:20:32.743
The damn oil shares from Kodor.


02:20:37.128 --> 02:20:39.416
Perhaps some day they'll make us rich.


02:20:52.962 --> 02:20:54.077
What's that'?


02:20:56.336 --> 02:20:57.581
A scent of melon?


02:20:59.836 --> 02:21:01.412
No, it's linseed oil!


02:21:01.878 --> 02:21:04.249
Yes, it is...


02:21:05.170 --> 02:21:08.251
Perhaps you know something
about vegetable oils, my good man?


02:21:09.296 --> 02:21:10.576
Oh, I certainly do.


02:21:11.128 --> 02:21:12.953
Well, well...
Who would have thought?


02:21:14.378 --> 02:21:15.575
Where are you from?


02:21:16.461 --> 02:21:18.168
From a small village near Arnhem.


02:21:19.170 --> 02:21:22.085
But it's a long time since
my childhood there.


02:21:22.670 --> 02:21:23.915
A very long time.


02:21:24.045 --> 02:21:27.659
Oh, interesting... that's where
my grandmother is from.


02:21:27.878 --> 02:21:29.123
Which village exactly?


02:21:29.962 --> 02:21:31.243
Rijjsen.


02:21:34.170 --> 02:21:36.457
And I thought you were
some sort of Fleming!


02:21:36.711 --> 02:21:37.873
My God, no!


02:21:38.920 --> 02:21:41.670
I haven't been home
for thirty years either.


02:21:44.128 --> 02:21:48.122
I'll have to die without having
tasted a good hut spot again...


02:21:49.586 --> 02:21:50.913
And bitterballen...


02:21:51.170 --> 02:21:52.829
Bitterballen, that's right.


02:21:52.962 --> 02:21:56.625
With a tad of cinnamon
from Ceylon... or curry...


02:22:02.878 --> 02:22:07.453
I need someone steady
on our East Indies line.


02:22:08.795 --> 02:22:10.999
I am not interested in
short term solutions.


02:22:12.420 --> 02:22:13.830
This is what
I am looking for.


02:22:14.003 --> 02:22:15.200
Good.


02:22:15.836 --> 02:22:20.044
It is the Jasmin a,
harboured in Cuxhaven...


02:22:20.795 --> 02:22:23.662
you should set sail in a week.
It is all right, I hope?


02:22:25.503 --> 02:22:28.668
I'd like to take my wife along.


02:22:30.336 --> 02:22:31.617
Your wife?


02:22:33.920 --> 02:22:35.994
Are you newlyweds or what?


02:22:36.128 --> 02:22:36.994
Not exactly.


02:22:38.545 --> 02:22:41.709
Or do you enjoy being with
your wife so much?


02:22:44.211 --> 02:22:45.492
Yes.


02:22:57.003 --> 02:22:58.460
It's so rare.


02:23:02.795 --> 02:23:06.160
I tend to place more trust
in lucky people...


02:23:08.211 --> 02:23:09.373
So...


02:23:09.711 --> 02:23:12.200
You'll set sail for Java
in a week then.


02:23:12.545 --> 02:23:14.287
Along with your wife.


02:23:21.003 --> 02:23:22.876
Am I dreaming or what...?


02:23:23.586 --> 02:23:25.127
Why don't you join us!


02:23:25.545 --> 02:23:27.002
We go to a costume ball!


02:23:28.086 --> 02:23:30.658
We are harem ladies and
we have no harem guard!


02:23:31.211 --> 02:23:32.124
Thank you.


02:23:47.629 --> 02:23:48.411
Lizzy?


02:25:30.211 --> 02:25:30.958
Champagne?


02:25:34.503 --> 02:25:35.250
Thank you.


02:27:45.503 --> 02:27:46.830
Well, well, well...


02:27:47.420 --> 02:27:49.542
We are sitting over there,
with Kodor.


02:27:50.461 --> 02:27:52.002
Won't you come and see him?


02:28:03.128 --> 02:28:04.704
The hell with him...


02:28:04.920 --> 02:28:07.670
Do come, or he'll be angry with me.


02:28:08.295 --> 02:28:08.911
Why not?


02:28:16.378 --> 02:28:18.997
What a surprise...


02:28:19.295 --> 02:28:21.618
Giacomo himself!


02:28:21.795 --> 02:28:24.497
Why are you eating
by your lonesome self?


02:28:25.170 --> 02:28:27.409
Got divorced, perhaps?


02:28:32.711 --> 02:28:34.252
I am...


02:28:37.503 --> 02:28:39.044
Yes, I did.


02:28:39.461 --> 02:28:40.374
Oh...


02:28:41.170 --> 02:28:42.710
We have to celebrate that!


02:29:06.003 --> 02:29:07.709
Do you know The Salty Sea?


02:29:16.253 --> 02:29:24.586
<i>We are sailing for a seafarer's pay
Over the salty sea</i>


02:29:26.045 --> 02:29:30.999
<i>Though there are never women on board</i>


02:29:31.211 --> 02:29:39.545
<i>Over the large and briny sea,
Over the salty sea</i>


02:29:41.086 --> 02:29:49.420
<i>And whether we're in a good mood or bad
Over the salty sea</i>


02:29:50.295 --> 02:29:54.668
<i>We are driven by the wind</i>


02:29:55.003 --> 02:30:01.912
<i>Over the large and briny sea,
Over the salty sea</i>


02:30:02.336 --> 02:30:09.045
<i>And we will get drunk ashore,
Over the salty sea</i>


02:30:09.461 --> 02:30:12.792
<i>The pour beer as bitter as bile</i>


02:30:13.170 --> 02:30:19.167
<i>Over the large and briny sea,
Over the salty sea</i>


02:30:19.420 --> 02:30:26.459
<i>And when we are gone forever,
over the salty sea</i>


02:30:27.086 --> 02:30:28.497
Very nice!


02:30:29.503 --> 02:30:31.826
Very virile, indeed...


02:30:33.711 --> 02:30:36.876
It's a pity your wife couldn't hear this.


02:30:37.586 --> 02:30:40.703
I wonder what is she doing right now.


02:30:54.253 --> 02:30:55.119
Have a nice trip!


02:31:01.295 --> 02:31:02.670
Who were those people?


02:31:04.795 --> 02:31:05.707
I have no idea.


02:31:05.920 --> 02:31:07.793
Was my wife in that car?


02:31:10.545 --> 02:31:11.706
Of course it was her.


02:31:11.878 --> 02:31:12.459
I... I...


02:31:13.670 --> 02:31:14.417
Where to?


02:31:14.670 --> 02:31:15.666
Central station.


02:32:01.836 --> 02:32:02.334
Captain...


02:32:13.586 --> 02:32:14.452
Good morning!


02:32:23.753 --> 02:32:25.708
Now hand over
those shares, please.


02:32:27.253 --> 02:32:28.119
What shares?


02:32:28.211 --> 02:32:29.669
The oil shares, what else.


02:32:30.628 --> 02:32:32.204
Let's not create
a scene over this.


02:32:58.003 --> 02:32:59.662
There's one more thing I need.


02:33:11.461 --> 02:33:13.037
Here, I'll dictate.


02:33:23.170 --> 02:33:24.912
With the help of my lover...


02:33:33.836 --> 02:33:36.408
I stole these shares from you.


02:33:43.170 --> 02:33:44.627
I'm sorry to admit...


02:33:49.295 --> 02:33:51.084
I lived a dishonorable life.


02:34:00.670 --> 02:34:01.915
Now sign it.


02:34:17.211 --> 02:34:18.243
Forgive me!


02:34:33.170 --> 02:34:34.663
I need it for the divorce.


02:34:38.295 --> 02:34:40.831
Because I'm not gonna
pay any alimony.


02:36:40.461 --> 02:36:47.703
<i>If I had a son, what would I say
to him by way of farewell?</i>


02:36:50.336 --> 02:36:53.999
<i>I would describe this morning,
maybe nothing else.</i>


02:36:54.711 --> 02:36:56.951
<i>That should be enough...</i>


02:36:57.086 --> 02:36:59.160
<i>One can't give advice anyway.</i>


02:37:01.211 --> 02:37:04.246
<i>I would talk to him
about evanescence...</i>


02:37:05.211 --> 02:37:09.621
<i>That life is nothing more
than playful variations.</i>


02:37:10.586 --> 02:37:13.834
<i>That it is useless to look
for something sublime behind it:</i>


02:37:14.753 --> 02:37:17.076
<i>a planned purpose
or a superior aim,</i>


02:37:17.420 --> 02:37:19.162
<i>because there is
nothing behind it.</i>


02:37:20.711 --> 02:37:23.793
<i>Because just as the light
slips away above us,</i>


02:37:24.045 --> 02:37:27.161
<i>in the same way life
slips away within us.</i>


02:37:38.711 --> 02:37:41.200
<i>So what would I say to my son?</i>


02:37:42.170 --> 02:37:45.749
<i>That he should learn to appreciate
this eternal procession...</i>


02:37:46.295 --> 02:37:52.541
<i>and not oppose it with all
his strength as I did at one time.</i>


02:37:54.086 --> 02:37:57.370
<i>Then he'll become the sort
of creature God had intended.</i>


02:37:58.378 --> 02:38:01.045
<i>One who lives easily,</i>


02:38:01.961 --> 02:38:04.794
<i>and passes on easily.</i>


02:38:47.711 --> 02:38:49.667
<i>- Hello?
- Good morning, Madame.</i>


02:38:50.253 --> 02:38:52.913
<i>- I'm an old acquaintance...
- Ah, is that you, Captain?</i>


02:38:53.461 --> 02:38:56.910
<i>How nice to hear your voice.
I recognized it right away!</i>


02:38:57.753 --> 02:39:00.538
<i>Do you remember that evening
at the cafe when we first met?</i>


02:39:00.628 --> 02:39:03.544
Believe it or not,
I even remember what we drank that evening.


02:39:05.211 --> 02:39:07.167
As a matter of fact,
I would like to...


02:39:07.295 --> 02:39:10.957
<i>And Lizzy, poor thing,
how sweet she was that evening...</i>


02:39:11.336 --> 02:39:13.955
<i>what a delightful little creature she was...</i>


02:39:14.420 --> 02:39:17.170
<i>Tell me, do you still think of her,
the poor dear?</i>


02:39:17.753 --> 02:39:19.708
Why do you keep saying
"the poor dear"?


02:39:21.211 --> 02:39:23.167
You've said it twice,
I don't understand.


02:39:24.461 --> 02:39:26.121
She doesn't seem miserable...


02:39:26.336 --> 02:39:28.292
I saw her in the street today.


02:39:29.211 --> 02:39:31.120
She didn't look like
she'd aged at all...


02:39:31.545 --> 02:39:32.244
<i>But...</i>


02:39:33.253 --> 02:39:34.498
<i>Sorry, but...</i>


02:39:35.378 --> 02:39:37.203
<i>who are you talking about?</i>


02:39:38.253 --> 02:39:39.710
Who do you think?


02:39:40.920 --> 02:39:43.752
I must tell you, seeing her
in that little black coat,


02:39:44.545 --> 02:39:46.038
it was funny because,


02:39:46.920 --> 02:39:49.622
you don't see that straight style
nowadays at all, but...


02:39:51.170 --> 02:39:53.160
her figure was the same as ever...


02:39:53.628 --> 02:39:56.460
<i>But, tell me, was the coat
closed at the neck?</i>


02:39:56.586 --> 02:39:57.867
Yes, it was closed...


02:39:58.836 --> 02:40:01.124
<i>And trimmed with fur?</i>


02:40:03.045 --> 02:40:04.206
Yes, yes...


02:40:05.420 --> 02:40:06.617
a light-colour fur.


02:40:07.170 --> 02:40:09.493
<i>Oh, God,
then it must have been her.</i>


02:40:09.920 --> 02:40:12.586
<i>Because I sent her that coat from Paris,</i>


02:40:13.253 --> 02:40:15.208
<i>just before she died...</i>


02:40:22.920 --> 02:40:24.165
I beg your pardon?


02:40:24.503 --> 02:40:25.830
<i>Didn't you know?</i>


02:40:26.878 --> 02:40:30.659
<i>Is it possible you didn't know
that the sweet dear has passed away?</i>


02:40:31.920 --> 02:40:33.626
<i>Six years ago now...</i>


02:40:35.170 --> 02:40:38.832
<i>But that's wonderful you see,
how lucky you are...</i>


02:40:39.378 --> 02:40:41.333
<i>What a shining little guest
you had today!</i>


02:40:42.045 --> 02:40:44.368
<i>And what a bright little
companion she was...</i>


02:40:44.586 --> 02:40:46.246
<i>while she lived beside you!</i>


02:40:47.170 --> 02:40:48.829
<i>She appeared to you today.</i>


02:40:49.920 --> 02:40:52.738
<i>After all,
she loved you so much.</i>

